"/en/docs/api-anthropic","content":"These two endpoints are compatible with Anthropic Messages and serve clients such as the Anthropic SDKs and Claude Code. The base address is `http://127.0.0.1:10600` (clients add `/v1/messages` themselves), authenticated with the model API key sent as `x-api-key` or `Authorization: Bearer` (see API overview). Usage examples are in Anthropic SDK.","locale":"en"},"8438":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-15","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","content":"Method and path","locale":"en"},"8439":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-16","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","content":"Purpose","locale":"en"},"8440":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-17","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","content":"`POST /v1/messages`","locale":"en"},"8441":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-18","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","content":"Generate a reply; JSON by default, SSE with `\"stream\": true`","locale":"en"},"8442":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-19","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","content":"`POST /v1/messages/count_tokens`","locale":"en"},"8443":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-20","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","content":"Count input tokens without generating a reply","locale":"en"},"8444":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-21","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","content":"Messages is stateless: send the whole conversation every time. Hoshimi keeps no history (some native upstream features may keep state of their own). Calls are recorded on the **Usage** page with the origin `messages`.","locale":"en"},"8445":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-22","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#request-validation","content":"Both endpoints check the outer shape of the request first and answer `400` (in Anthropic's shape) when it fails:","locale":"en"},"8446":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-23","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#request-validation","content":"`model` is a non-empty string. Messages does not use the default model.","locale":"en"},"8447":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-24","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#request-validation","content":"`messages` is a non-empty array; each message has a string `role`, and `content` is a string or an array.","locale":"en"},"8448":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-25","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#request-validation","content":"`stream`, when present, is a boolean.","locale":"en"},"8449":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-26","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#request-validation","content":"`max_tokens` is a non-negative integer (optional for `count_tokens`).","locale":"en"},"8450":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-27","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#request-validation","content":"`tools`, when present, is an array.","locale":"en"},"8451":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-28","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#request-validation","content":"Extension fields are not checked here: native forwarding leaves them to the upstream, and protocol conversion checks them as described below.","locale":"en"},"8452":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-29","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#native-forwarding-or-protocol-conversion","content":"Hoshimi finds the provider through model routing, then looks at the accounts of that provider that can serve the model:","locale":"en"},"8453":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-30","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#native-forwarding-or-protocol-conversion","content":"If the provider has a Messages endpoint of its own for them (models whose protocol is Messages on a regular API provider, such as `anthropic` or `minimax-api`), the request is **forwarded natively**, rotating across those accounts.","locale":"en"},"8454":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-31","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#native-forwarding-or-protocol-conversion","content":"Otherwise it goes through **protocol conversion**. Dedicated providers with custom envelopes always use their own translators.","locale":"en"},"8455":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-32","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#native-forwarding-or-protocol-conversion","content":"The decision rests on each account's actual protocol and endpoint, not just a model's capability label. A native failure never quietly falls back to conversion.","locale":"en"},"8456":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-33","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#native-forwarding-or-protocol-conversion","content":"These provider options (in `providers.<id>.options`) adjust the behaviour:","locale":"en"},"8457":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-34","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#native-forwarding-or-protocol-conversion","content":"Option","locale":"en"},"8458":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-35","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#native-forwarding-or-protocol-conversion","content":"Effect","locale":"en"},"8459":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-36","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#native-forwarding-or-protocol-conversion","content":"`messages_passthrough: false`","locale":"en"},"8460":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-37","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#native-forwarding-or-protocol-conversion","content":"No native forwarding; force conversion, for a Messages provider with special requirements","locale":"en"},"8461":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-38","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#native-forwarding-or-protocol-conversion","content":"`messages_count_tokens: true`","locale":"en"},"8462":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-39","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#native-forwarding-or-protocol-conversion","content":"Use the upstream's native counting endpoint for `count_tokens`; on by default for `anthropic`, off for other providers","locale":"en"},"8463":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-40","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#native-forwarding-or-protocol-conversion","content":"`structured_outputs: true`","locale":"en"},"8464":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-41","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#native-forwarding-or-protocol-conversion","content":"Let the conversion path turn `output_config.format` into the upstream's structured output; enable only when the upstream and its models support it","locale":"en"},"8465":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-42","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#native-forwarding","content":"The body goes out unchanged except that `model` becomes the upstream model name (`count_tokens` also drops `stream`). System arrays, content order, opaque signatures, tools, cache markers, `context_management`, structured output and future fields are all left for the upstream to validate.","locale":"en"},"8466":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-43","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#native-forwarding","content":"The client's `anthropic-*` headers and query parameters go along. Upstream credentials come from the selected account; the key the client sent to the gateway is never forwarded. The `anthropic-beta` capabilities an OAuth account requires are merged with the client's.","locale":"en"},"8467":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-44","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#native-forwarding","content":"The response keeps `content-type`, `request-id`, `x-request-id`, `retry-after` (rounded up to whole seconds), `x-should-retry` and every `anthropic-*` header.","locale":"en"},"8468":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-45","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#native-forwarding","content":"A streaming response keeps the upstream's SSE frame by frame, unknown events, usage, signatures and pings included; Hoshimi inserts its own `ping` only between complete frames, never inside partial JSON. Non-streaming JSON is returned as it came.","locale":"en"},"8469":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-46","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#native-forwarding","content":"If the upstream stream ends without `message_stop` or `error`, or breaks off mid-frame, Hoshimi reports an error rather than a clean finish.","locale":"en"},"8470":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-47","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#native-forwarding","content":"When the client disconnects, Hoshimi closes the upstream connection; a stream that has begun is not replayed on another account.","locale":"en"},"8471":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-48","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#native-forwarding","content":"Upstream errors keep their status, body, request id and protocol headers (`x-should-retry`, `retry-after`, `anthropic-ratelimit-*` among them). An explicit `x-should-retry: false` from the upstream stops Hoshimi from retrying on another account.","locale":"en"},"8472":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-49","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#native-forwarding","content":"Being forwarded is not the same as being supported: an Anthropic-shaped endpoint can still reject features it does not implement, and its original error reaches the client.","locale":"en"},"8473":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-50","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#protocol-conversion","content":"The conversion path turns a Messages request into an internal Chat request, hands it to the provider's adapter, and turns the result back into Messages.","locale":"en"},"8474":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-51","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#request-fields","content":"Field","locale":"en"},"8475":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-52","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#request-fields","content":"Handling","locale":"en"},"8476":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-53","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#request-fields","content":"`system`","locale":"en"},"8477":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-54","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#request-fields","content":"A string or an array of text blocks, becoming a system message; text only","locale":"en"},"8478":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-55","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#request-fields","content":"`messages[].role`","locale":"en"},"8479":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-56","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#request-fields","content":"`user` or `assistant` only; a `system`-role message is refused (`Messages roles must be user or assistant; use top-level system.`)","locale":"en"},"8480":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-57","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#request-fields","content":"`max_tokens`","locale":"en"},"8481":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-58","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#request-fields","content":"Must be a positive integer","locale":"en"},"8482":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-59","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#request-fields","content":"`temperature`, `top_p`","locale":"en"},"8483":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-60","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#request-fields","content":"Numbers, passed through","locale":"en"},"8484":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-61","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#request-fields","content":"`top_k`","locale":"en"},"8485":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-62","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#request-fields","content":"Passed only to models whose upstream protocol is Messages","locale":"en"},"8486":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-63","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#request-fields","content":"`stop_sequences`","locale":"en"},"8487":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-64","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#request-fields","content":"Becomes `stop`","locale":"en"},"8488":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-65","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#request-fields","content":"`tools`","locale":"en"},"8489":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-66","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#request-fields","content":"Custom tools only (`type` absent or `custom`) with `name` and `input_schema`; `description` and `strict` are kept; server tool types are refused","locale":"en"},"8490":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-67","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#request-fields","content":"`tool_choice`","locale":"en"},"8491":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-68","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#request-fields","content":"`auto` → `auto`, `any` → `required`, `none` → `none`, `tool` → a named function (which must be declared); `any` and `tool` need declared tools; `disable_parallel_tool_use` becomes `parallel_tool_calls`","locale":"en"},"8492":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-69","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#request-fields","content":"`thinking`","locale":"en"},"8493":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-70","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#request-fields","content":"`type` is `enabled`, `disabled` or `adaptive`; an `enabled` `budget_tokens` is at least 1024 and less than `max_tokens`","locale":"en"},"8494":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-71","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#request-fields","content":"`output_config.effort`","locale":"en"},"8495":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-72","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#request-fields","content":"`low`, `medium`, `high`, `xhigh`, `max`","locale":"en"},"8496":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-73","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#request-fields","content":"`output_config.format`","locale":"en"},"8497":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-74","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#request-fields","content":"Needs `structured_outputs` on the provider; the JSON Schema becomes Chat `response_format` (or Responses `text.format`)","locale":"en"},"8498":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-75","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#request-fields","content":"`output_config.task_budget`","locale":"en"},"8499":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-76","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#request-fields","content":"Refused; needs a native upstream","locale":"en"},"8500":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-77","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#request-fields","content":"`metadata`","locale":"en"},"8501":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-78","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#request-fields","content":"Must be an object; `metadata.user_id` becomes `user`","locale":"en"},"8502":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-79","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#request-fields","content":"`mcp_servers`, `container`, `context_management`","locale":"en"},"8503":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-80","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#request-fields","content":"Refused: `… requires a native Messages upstream.`","locale":"en"},"8504":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-81","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#request-fields","content":"Conversion errors are prefixed with the provider id, for example `opencode: context_management requires a native Messages upstream.`.","locale":"en"},"8505":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-82","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#content-blocks","content":"Block","locale":"en"},"8506":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-83","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[]