cs/api-anthropic-121","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#effort-mapping","content":"`high`","locale":"en"},"8545":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-122","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#effort-mapping","content":"When both are present, `output_config.effort` wins. For models whose upstream protocol is Messages, `thinking`, `output_config` and `metadata` are passed through.","locale":"en"},"8546":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-123","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#response","content":"Content blocks may be, in order, `thinking` (with a `signature`), `redacted_thinking`, `text` and `tool_use`.","locale":"en"},"8547":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-124","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#response","content":"`stop_reason` is `end_turn`, `max_tokens`, `tool_use`, `stop_sequence` or `refusal`; it is `tool_use` when there are tool calls and the upstream reported a normal finish.","locale":"en"},"8548":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-125","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#response","content":"In `usage`, `input_tokens` excludes the cache; cache reads and writes are in `cache_read_input_tokens` and `cache_creation_input_tokens`.","locale":"en"},"8549":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-126","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#response","content":"The `request-id` response header equals the message `id` (`msg_…`).","locale":"en"},"8550":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-127","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#response","content":"Cache markers survive only native forwarding; conversion does not promise equivalent caching. Semantics such as tool examples are likewise fully kept only by native forwarding.","locale":"en"},"8551":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-128","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#thinking-signatures","content":"In a multi-turn conversation, the client sends the assistant's `thinking` / `redacted_thinking` blocks back with their original signatures and tool calls:","locale":"en"},"8552":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-129","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#thinking-signatures","content":"Native forwarding hands these blocks to the upstream untouched, without reconstruction.","locale":"en"},"8553":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-130","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#thinking-signatures","content":"On conversion, reasoning details from non-Anthropic upstreams (encrypted reasoning, for instance) are encoded into a Hoshimi signature: the prefix `hoshimi:v1:` followed by base64url-encoded JSON. When the next request brings the signature back, Hoshimi decodes it and hands the original data to the upstream.","locale":"en"},"8554":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-131","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#thinking-signatures","content":"A signature over 1 MiB, or one that does not decode, answers `400`.","locale":"en"},"8555":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-132","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#thinking-signatures","content":"Do not synthesise or edit signatures, and do not reuse one model's or provider's signature for another. A signature preserves protocol data; it is not a promise that every upstream supports thinking.","locale":"en"},"8556":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-133","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#stream-events","content":"With `\"stream\": true`, each event is sent as two lines, `event: <type>` and `data: <json>`:","locale":"en"},"8557":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-134","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#stream-events","content":"Event","locale":"en"},"8558":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-135","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#stream-events","content":"Content","locale":"en"},"8559":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-136","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#stream-events","content":"`message_start`","locale":"en"},"8560":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-137","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#stream-events","content":"The message object (`id`, `model`, empty `content`)","locale":"en"},"8561":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-138","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#stream-events","content":"`content_block_start`","locale":"en"},"8562":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-139","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#stream-events","content":"A block begins: `text`, `thinking`, `redacted_thinking` or `tool_use`","locale":"en"},"8563":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-140","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#stream-events","content":"`content_block_delta`","locale":"en"},"8564":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-141","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#stream-events","content":"`text_delta`, `thinking_delta`, `signature_delta` or `input_json_delta`","locale":"en"},"8565":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-142","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#stream-events","content":"`content_block_stop`","locale":"en"},"8566":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-143","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#stream-events","content":"A block ends","locale":"en"},"8567":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-144","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#stream-events","content":"`message_delta`","locale":"en"},"8568":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-145","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#stream-events","content":"`stop_reason`, `stop_sequence` and the final `usage`","locale":"en"},"8569":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-146","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#stream-events","content":"`message_stop`","locale":"en"},"8570":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-147","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#stream-events","content":"The end","locale":"en"},"8571":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-148","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#stream-events","content":"`ping`","locale":"en"},"8572":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-149","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#stream-events","content":"Every 15 seconds while waiting on the upstream, only between complete events","locale":"en"},"8573":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-150","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#stream-events","content":"`error`","locale":"en"},"8574":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-151","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#stream-events","content":"A failure in the stream, in Anthropic's error shape","locale":"en"},"8575":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-152","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#stream-events","content":"A streaming request gets the first piece of data from the upstream before sending response headers, so authentication and rate-limit failures still come back with their real HTTP status rather than `200` plus an error event.","locale":"en"},"8576":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-153","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#token-counting","content":"`POST /v1/messages/count_tokens`","locale":"en"},"8577":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-154","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#token-counting","content":"When the provider declares a native counting endpoint (`anthropic` by default; others with `messages_count_tokens: true`), the body and protocol headers are forwarded and the upstream's count returned.","locale":"en"},"8578":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-155","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#token-counting","content":"When none is declared, or the native endpoint answers `404`, `405` or `501`, Hoshimi returns a local estimate with the header `x-hoshimi-token-count: estimate`. The estimate approximates from the UTF-8 size of `system`, `messages`, `tools` and `tool_choice` (about one token per 3 bytes, at least 1), accepts native document and tool blocks, and runs no tokenizer.","locale":"en"},"8579":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-156","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#token-counting","content":"Authentication, quota and server errors are not hidden behind an estimate; they come back as errors.","locale":"en"},"8580":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-157","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#token-counting","content":"`max_tokens` is optional. Counting generates no reply and adds no usage record.","locale":"en"},"8581":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-158","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#errors","content":"Every error uses Anthropic's shape:","locale":"en"},"8582":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-159","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#errors","content":"A body that does not parse against the endpoint's schema: `400`, `Invalid Messages request body.`.","locale":"en"},"8583":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-160","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#errors","content":"Errors the gateway raises itself (validation, routing, conversion) use Anthropic's shape, with `error.type` following the status (see API overview).","locale":"en"},"8584":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-161","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#errors","content":"Upstream errors on native forwarding keep the upstream's status, body and protocol headers.","locale":"en"},"8585":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-162","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#errors","content":"Failures after the stream has begun arrive as an `error` event.","locale":"en"},"8586":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-163","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#protocol-references","content":"Messages HTTP reference","locale":"en"},"8587":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-164","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#protocol-references","content":"Claude Code gateway compatibility","locale":"en"},"8588":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-165","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#protocol-references","content":"Streaming events","locale":"en"},"8589":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-166","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#protocol-references","content":"Tool search and references","locale":"en"},"8590":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-167","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#protocol-references","content":"Effort","locale":"en"},"8591":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-168","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#protocol-references","content":"The development extra includes the official Anthropic SDK. Protocol tests run real SDK JSON and streaming helpers against local mock upstreams, covering account rotation, signature replay, counting, heartbeats, cancellation and truncation. Whether a given account works, or a model supports a given feature, needs checking separately.","locale":"en"},"8592":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","type":"page","content":"Management API","breadcrumbs":["Hoshimi Documentation","API reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/api-management","locale":"en"},"8593":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-0","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management","content":"Every /api/v1 management endpoint the Web UI uses: app information, settings, providers and accounts, the model catalogue, availability probes, credential renewal, balances and check-in, sign-in, usage statistics, with each endpoint's method, purpose and authentication.","locale":"en"},"8594":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-1","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/api-management#endpoints","content":"Endpoints","locale":"en"},"8595":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-2","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/api-management#app","content":"App","locale":"en"},"8596":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-3","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/api-management#settings","content":"Settings","locale":"en"},"8597":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-4","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/api-management#providers-and-accounts","content":"Providers and accounts","locale":"en"},"8598":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-5","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/ap