ted with the model API key (see API overview). Usage examples are in OpenAI SDKs and curl.","locale":"en"},"8817":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-14","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai","content":"Method and path","locale":"en"},"8818":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-15","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai","content":"Purpose","locale":"en"},"8819":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-16","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai","content":"`POST /v1/chat/completions`","locale":"en"},"8820":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-17","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai","content":"Chat Completions; streams when `stream` is absent","locale":"en"},"8821":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-18","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai","content":"`POST /v1/responses`","locale":"en"},"8822":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-19","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai","content":"Responses, stateless, converted to Chat internally; streams when `stream` is absent","locale":"en"},"8823":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-20","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai","content":"`GET /v1/models`","locale":"en"},"8824":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-21","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai","content":"The model catalogue","locale":"en"},"8825":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-22","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai","content":"`GET /v1/classifiers`","locale":"en"},"8826":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-23","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai","content":"Available classifiers","locale":"en"},"8827":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-24","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai","content":"`POST /v1/classify`","locale":"en"},"8828":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-25","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai","content":"Answer questions with a classifier","locale":"en"},"8829":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-26","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai","content":"The inference endpoints and `/v1/messages` share one model catalogue and the same account rotation, retries and usage recording. Every call is recorded on the **Usage** page, with the origin `chat`, `responses` or `classify`.","locale":"en"},"8830":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-27","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#chat-completions","content":"`POST /v1/chat/completions`","locale":"en"},"8831":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-28","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#request","content":"The body is a standard Chat Completions object. The fields Hoshimi reads itself:","locale":"en"},"8832":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-29","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#request","content":"Field","locale":"en"},"8833":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-30","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#request","content":"Notes","locale":"en"},"8834":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-31","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#request","content":"`model`","locale":"en"},"8835":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-32","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#request","content":"The model name; see \"Model routing\" below. When absent, `server.default_model` is used; with no default model either, the answer is `400` (`Missing 'model' field.`)","locale":"en"},"8836":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-33","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#request","content":"`messages`","locale":"en"},"8837":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-34","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#request","content":"The whole conversation; Hoshimi keeps no history","locale":"en"},"8838":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-35","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#request","content":"`stream`","locale":"en"},"8839":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-36","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#request","content":"Defaults to `true`. Send `false` explicitly to get one JSON object","locale":"en"},"8840":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-37","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#request","content":"`reasoning_effort`","locale":"en"},"8841":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-38","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#request","content":"The effort level; see \"Reasoning effort\" below","locale":"en"},"8842":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-39","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#request","content":"`max_tokens` / `max_completion_tokens`","locale":"en"},"8843":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-40","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#request","content":"The output ceiling; rewritten by the effort budget when an effort is given, see below","locale":"en"},"8844":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-41","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#request","content":"`tools` / `tool_choice`","locale":"en"},"8845":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-42","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#request","content":"`function` tools; `tool_choice` is `auto`, `none`, `required` or a named function","locale":"en"},"8846":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-43","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#request","content":"Other fields (`temperature`, `top_p`, `stop` and so on) go to the upstream's adapter, and whether they take effect depends on the upstream protocol and model. Message content may include `image_url` parts (a `data:` URL or an HTTP(S) address); only models that read images understand them.","locale":"en"},"8847":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-44","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#non-streaming-response","content":"`model` echoes the model name from the request, `provider/` prefix included.","locale":"en"},"8848":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-45","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#non-streaming-response","content":"`message` may also carry `reasoning_content` (the reasoning text), `reasoning_details` (structured reasoning data from the upstream) and `tool_calls`.","locale":"en"},"8849":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-46","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#non-streaming-response","content":"`finish_reason` is `stop`, `tool_calls` or `length`.","locale":"en"},"8850":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-47","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#non-streaming-response","content":"The `usage` details depend on what the upstream reports; with no usage from the upstream every count is `0`.","locale":"en"},"8851":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-48","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#streaming-response","content":"The first chunk carries only `role`. Later `delta`s carry `content`, `reasoning_content`, `reasoning_details` or `tool_calls`.","locale":"en"},"8852":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-49","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#streaming-response","content":"A tool call's first chunk has its `id`, `type` and `function.name`; later chunks append `function.arguments` by `index`.","locale":"en"},"8853":{"id":"/en/docs/api