penai#reasoning-effort","content":"`max`","locale":"en"},"8954":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-151","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"If the result is still not on the menu, the model's default level is used. The chosen level is written into the upstream request the way the model declares; the output ceiling is then the smaller of the model's capacity and the request's own value, whatever the level.","locale":"en"},"8955":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-152","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"**Other reasoning models** use Hoshimi's three output budgets (one ceiling shared by thinking and the answer):","locale":"en"},"8956":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-153","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"Level","locale":"en"},"8957":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-154","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"Written in the request as","locale":"en"},"8958":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-155","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"Output ceiling","locale":"en"},"8959":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-156","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"`light`","locale":"en"},"8960":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-157","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"`light`, `minimal`, `low`","locale":"en"},"8961":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-158","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"2048","locale":"en"},"8962":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-159","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"`balanced` (default)","locale":"en"},"8963":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-160","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"`balanced`, `medium`, and anything unrecognised","locale":"en"},"8964":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-161","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"8192","locale":"en"},"8965":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-162","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"`deep`","locale":"en"},"8966":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-163","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"`deep`, `high`, `xhigh`, `max`","locale":"en"},"8967":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-164","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"The model's maximum output","locale":"en"},"8968":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-165","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"For a model whose thinking cannot be turned off, each ceiling is doubled.","locale":"en"},"8969":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-166","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"The ceiling never exceeds the model's maximum output or the request's own `max_tokens`, and never drops below 512.","locale":"en"},"8970":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-167","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"For these models the `reasoning_effort` / `reasoning` fields are not sent upstream; only `max_tokens` controls the budget.","locale":"en"},"8971":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-168","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"For a model that neither reasons nor has a thinking menu, Hoshimi leaves the effort fields alone and passes them to the upstream as they are. Each model's levels and default are on the **Models** page, or in `efforts` and `effort_default` of `GET /api/v1/models`.","locale":"en"},"8972":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-169","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#classification","content":"TypeSafe classifiers are not chat models. They are not in `/v1/models` and are used through their own endpoints (with an account on the `typesafe` provider).","locale":"en"},"8973":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-170","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#classification","content":"The body sent to `POST /v1/classify`:","locale":"en"},"8974":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-171","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#classification","content":"`model` must be an id from `/v1/classifiers`; otherwise the answer is `404` (`Select a classifier from /v1/classifiers.`).","locale":"en"},"8975":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-172","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#classification","content":"`state` is an object and `questions` a non-empty object; each question's `type` is `bool`, `score` or `choice`, and its other fields go to the upstream unchanged. Images are not supported.","locale":"en"},"8976":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-173","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#classification","content":"The response is `{\"provider\", \"model\", \"answers\", \"usage\"}`: a `bool` answer is `{\"type\": \"bool\", \"probability\": …}`; a `score` answer carries `score` and `confidence`; a `choice` answer carries `choice`, `probabilities` and `confidence`.","locale":"en"},"8977":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","type":"page","content":"Playground API","breadcrumbs":["Hoshimi Documentation","API reference"