":"`compaction`","locale":"en"},"9274":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-296","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#the-event-stream","content":"`step`","locale":"en"},"9275":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-297","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#the-event-stream","content":"The conversation being compacted; replace the step with the same `id`","locale":"en"},"9276":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-298","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#the-event-stream","content":"`done`","locale":"en"},"9277":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-299","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#the-event-stream","content":"`message`","locale":"en"},"9278":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-300","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#the-event-stream","content":"Last: the reply as kept, with its `status` and `error`","locale":"en"},"9279":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-301","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#the-event-stream","content":"`reasoning` and `delta` add to the last step when it is of their kind, and start a new step otherwise. While nothing else comes (a tool runs, or waits for approval), a comment line `: ping` goes out every 2 seconds; skip lines that start with `:`.","locale":"en"},"9280":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-302","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#the-event-stream","content":"A reply with one tool call looks like this (messages shortened):","locale":"en"},"9281":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-303","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#the-event-stream","content":"How a stream ends:","locale":"en"},"9282":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-304","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#the-event-stream","content":"Errors found before the question is kept (no model, an unknown `parent_id` or attachment) are a plain `400` or `404`, not a stream.","locale":"en"},"9283":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-305","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#the-event-stream","content":"An error from the model or the station after that settles the reply as `error`, and the stream still ends with `done`.","locale":"en"},"9284":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-306","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#the-event-stream","content":"Closing the connection only stops reading: the reply goes on on the server, and is kept as it ends. Follow it again with `GET /conversations/{id}/events` (below).","locale":"en"},"9285":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-307","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#the-event-stream","content":"`POST /conversations/{id}/stop` stops it: a running tool is told to stop, a waiting approval is dropped, and the reply is kept as `stopped` with what came so far. Every stream following it ends with that `done`.","locale":"en"},"9286":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-308","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#replies-in-the-background","content":"A reply (and a compaction, `POST .../compact`) runs on the server whether or not a client reads it, and a conversation has one at a time: a send, a retry or a compaction while one runs is `409`. The conversation's `running` says one runs, and `waiting` that it waits for an approval; the list says so too, for every conversation.","locale":"en"},"9287":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-309","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#replies-in-the-background","content":"`GET /conversations/{id}/events` streams the reply under way from its first event (`?after=n` skips the first `n`), exactly as its send streamed them, then the rest as they come, to its `done`. Any number of clients can follow it at once. With none running it is `404`: the reply has ended, and `GET /conversations/{id}` holds it as kept.","locale":"en"},"9288":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-310","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#replies-in-the-background","content":"A reply that completes while nothing follows it names a conversation still without a title, as `POST .../title` would.","locale":"en"},"9289":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-311","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#retry","content":"`POST /conversations/{id}/messages/{message_id}/retry` streams another reply, with the same events except `user`. `message_id` is a reply (the new one goes beside it) or a question left unanswered (it gets its first reply).","locale":"en"},"9290":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-312","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#retry","content":"Field","locale":"en"},"9291":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-313","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#retry","content":"Default","locale":"en"},"9292":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-314","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#retry","content":"`model`","locale":"en"},"9293":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-315","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#retry","content":"The retried reply's model; for a question, the conversation's","locale":"en"},"9294":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-316","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#retry","content":"`effort`","locale":"en"},"9295":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-317","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#retry","content":"The retried reply's effort; for a question, the conversation's. `\"\"` sends none","locale":"en"},"9296":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-318","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#steps","content":"A reply that called a tool or was steered keeps its `steps`, in order. Every step has a `type` and a `round` (from 0, one per round of tool calls):","locale":"en"},"9297":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-319","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#steps","content":"`type`","locale":"en"},"9298":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-320","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#steps","content":"Fields","locale":"en"},"9299":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-321","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#steps","content":"`reasoning`","locale":"en"},"9300":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-322","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#steps","content":"`text`, `ms` (how long it reasoned)","locale":"en"},"9301":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-323","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#steps","content":"`text`","locale":"en"},"9302":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-324","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#steps","content":"`text`","locale":"en"},"9303":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-325","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#steps","content":"`user`","locale":"en"},"9304":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-326","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#steps","content":"`id`, `text`: a message sent with `/steer`, read at the start of this round","locale":"en"},"9305":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-327","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#steps","content":"`compaction`","locale":"en"},"9306":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-328","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#steps","content":"`id`, `status` (`running`, `done`, `failed`, `stopped`), `trigger` (`auto`, `overflow`, `manual`), `phase` (`pre-turn`, `mid-turn`, `manual`), `summary`, `recent` (your messages kept verbatim), `tokens_before`, `tokens_after`, `model` (that wrote it), `ms`, `error`, `at`: the conversation compacted before this round","locale":"en"},"9307":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-329","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#steps","content":"`tool`","locale":"en"},"9308":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-330","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#steps","content":"`id`, `name`, `arguments` (the JSON string the model wrote), `status`, `output`, `exit_code`, `ms`, `meta`, `approval`, `review`","locale":"en"},"9309":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-331","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#steps","content":"A tool step's `status`:","locale":"en"},"9310":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-332","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#steps","content":"`status`","locale":"en"},"9311":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-333","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#steps","content":"Meaning","locale":"en"},"9312":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-334","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#steps","content":"`pending`","locale":"en"},"9313":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-335","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#steps","content":"The model is still writing the call; `arguments` is complete once the round ends","locale":"en"},"9314":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-336","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#steps","content":"`reviewing`","locale":"en"},"9315":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-337","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#steps","content":"Being judged by the review model (**Automatic review**); `approval` says why it needs approval, as for `waiting`. Then `running`, `denied`, or `waiting` when the review came to no decision","locale":"en"},"9316":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-338","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#steps","content":"`waiting`","locale":"en"},"9317":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-339","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#steps","content":"Waiting for the user's approval; `approval` says why: `command`, `edit`, `edit-outside` or `read-outside`","locale":"en"},"9318":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-340","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#steps","content":"`running`","locale":"en"},"9319":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-341","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#steps","content":"Running","locale":"en"},"9320":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-342","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#steps","content":"`done`","locale":"en"},"9321":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-343","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#steps","content":"Finished","locale":"en"},"9322":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-344","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#steps","content":"`error`","locale":"en"},"9323":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-345","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#steps","content":"Failed (a non-zero exit, bad arguments, an unknown tool); `output` says why","locale":"en"},"9324":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-346","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#steps","content":"`denied`","locale":"en"},"9325":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-347","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#steps","content":"The user or the review model denied it; it did not run. Denied by the review model, `output` is what the model was told; denied by the user, it is empty","locale":"en"},"9326":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-348","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#steps","content":"`stopped`","locale":"en"},"9327":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-349","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#steps","content":"The reply was stopped first (or, on replies from before rounds of tool calls became unlimited, it hit its round limit)","locale":"en"},"9328":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-350","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#steps","content":"`output` is what the model was sent (at most 32,000 characters). `meta` carries what the page shows beside it:","locale":"en"},"9329":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-351","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#steps","content":"Tool","locale":"en"},"9330":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-352","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#steps","content":"`meta`","locale":"en"},"9331":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-353","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#steps","content":"`read`","locale":"en"},"9332":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-354","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#steps","content":"`path`, and `lines`, `from`, `to` for a file or `entries` for a folder","locale":"en"},"9333":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-355","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#steps","content":"`apply_patch`","locale":"en"},"9334":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-356","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#steps","content":"`files`: each `path`, `kind` (`add`, `update`, `delete`) and `from` when moved","locale":"en"},"9335":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-357","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#steps","content":"`shell`","locale":"en"},"9336":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-358","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#steps","content":"`cwd`, `shell` (the shell it ran in), `timed_out`","locale":"en"},"9337":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-359","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#steps","content":"`exec_command`, `write_stdin`","locale":"en"},"9338":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-360","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#steps","content":"`session_id`, `running`, `cwd`, `shell`; `exec_command` also `command`","locale":"en"},"9339":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-361","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#steps","content":"`kill_session`","locale":"en"},"9340":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-362","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#steps","content":"`session_id`","locale":"en"},"9341":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-363","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#steps","content":"`web_search`","locale":"en"},"9342":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-364","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#steps","content":"`query`, `results`","locale":"en"},"9343":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-365","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#steps","content":"`web_fetch`","locale":"en"},"9344":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-366","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#steps","content":"`url` (the final address), `title`","locale":"en"},"9345":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-367","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#steps","content":"A tool step's `review` is `null` until the review model has judged it, then `{\"outcome\", \"risk_level\", \"user_authorization\", \"rationale\", \"model\", \"ms\", \"failed\"}`: `outcome` `allow` or `deny`, `risk_level` `low`, `medium`, `high` or `critical`, `user_authorization` `unknown`, `low`, `medium` or `high`, `model` the reviewer, `ms` how long it took. When the review came to no decision and the call went to the user, `failed` is `true`, `outcome` is empty and `rationale` says why.","locale":"en"},"9346":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-368","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#steps","content":"A call that was stopped while running also has `\"cancelled\": true`. When the conversation is sent to a model again, each round becomes its steering messages, an assistant message with its `tool_calls`, and a `tool` message per call; with no tools on, the calls and their results go as text.","locale":"en"},"9347":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-369","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#approvals","content":"A `tool` event with `status` `waiting` asks for an answer. Send it with the step's `id`:","locale":"en"},"9348":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-370","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#approvals","content":"`decision`","locale":"en"},"9349":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-371","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#approvals","content":"Effect","locale":"en"},"9350":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-372","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#approvals","content":"`allow`","locale":"en"},"9351":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-373","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#approvals","content":"Run this call","locale":"en"},"9352":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-374","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#approvals","content":"`always`","locale":"en"},"9353":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-375","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#approvals","content":"Run it, and stop asking for this tool switch in this conversation (inside and outside the workspace count separately) until the server restarts","locale":"en"},"9354":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-376","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#approvals","content":"`deny`","locale":"en"},"9355":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-377","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#approvals","content":"Skip it; the model is told the user declined","locale":"en"},"9356":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-378","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#approvals","content":"Only `waiting` calls take an answer; a `reviewing` one is the review model's. The answer is `204`; `404` when no such call waits. A call waits 10 minutes, then counts as denied. The stream then carries the call's next state. Which calls wait depends on the approval mode (see Playground tools).","locale":"en"},"9357":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-379","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#steering","content":"`POST /conversations/{id}/steer` with `{\"content\": \"...\"}` sends a message to the reply under way, without stopping it. It answers `202` with `{\"id\": \"steer_…\"}`.","locale":"en"},"9358":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-380","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#steering","content":"The model reads it at the start of its next round, after the calls in progress; the stream then sends a `steer` event whose step has that `id`.","locale":"en"},"9359":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-381","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#steering","content":"One sent as the model finishes keeps the reply going for another round, to answer it.","locale":"en"},"9360":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-382","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#steering","content":"`409` when no reply can take it: none is running, the running one has no tools, or it has just ended. Send it as a new message then.","locale":"en"},"9361":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-383","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#steering","content":"`400` for an empty message.","locale":"en"},"9362":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-384","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#steering","content":"A message queued when the reply stops or fails is never read.","locale":"en"},"9363":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-385","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#background-commands","content":"`GET /conversations/{id}/terminals` lists the background commands (`exec_command` sessions) the conversation's tools started that are running, or have exited and not yet been read by the model:","locale":"en"},"9364":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-386","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#background-commands","content":"`DELETE /conversations/{id}/terminals/{session_id}` stops one and everything it started (`204`; `404` when it is not this conversation's). They also stop when the conversation is deleted and when the server stops.","locale":"en"},"9365":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-387","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#attachments","content":"Upload a file first, then send its `id` in `attachment_ids`. The request body is the file itself:","locale":"en"},"9366":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-388","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#attachments","content":"Query","locale":"en"},"9367":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-389","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#attachments","content":"Meaning","locale":"en"},"9368":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-390","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#attachments","content":"`name`","locale":"en"},"9369":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-391","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#attachments","content":"The file's name (required)","locale":"en"},"9370":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-392","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#attachments","content":"`type`","locale":"en"},"9371":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-393","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#attachments","content":"The file's own type, when the body is its extracted text (the Web UI sends a PDF's text with `type=application/pdf`)","locale":"en"},"9372":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-394","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#attachments","content":"`width`, `height`","locale":"en"},"9373":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-395","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#attachments","content":"An image's size, optional","locale":"en"},"9374":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-396","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#attachments","content":"The `Content-Type` decides how it is kept: `image/png`, `image/jpeg`, `image/webp` or `image/gif` as an image; any `text/*` type, or `application/json`, `xml`, `yaml`, `x-yaml`, `javascript`, `x-sh`, `sql` or `toml`, as UTF-8 text. Anything else, or an empty body, is a `400`. The server keeps what it is given: scaling images down and extracting PDF text are done by the Web UI before upload. A model is sent at most 200,000 characters of a file's text.","locale":"en"},"9375":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-397","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#attachments","content":"The answer is the attachment: `id`, `kind`, `name`, `mime`, `size`, `width`, `height`.","locale":"en"},"9376":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-398","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#attachments","content":"`GET /attachments/{id}` returns an image with its own type, a file as `text/plain`.","locale":"en"},"9377":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-399","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#attachments","content":"`DELETE /attachments/{id}` takes back an attachment before it is sent (`204`); one a message carries is a `400`.","locale":"en"},"9378":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-400","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#attachments","content":"An attachment never sent is deleted after a day.","locale":"en"},"9379":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-401","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#context-and-compaction","content":"`GET /conversations/{id}/context` says how full the conversation on screen is against its model's context window:","locale":"en"},"9380":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-402","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#context-and-compaction","content":"Field","locale":"en"},"9381":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-403","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#context-and-compaction","content":"Meaning","locale":"en"},"9382":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-404","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#context-and-compaction","content":"`model`, `provider`, `effort`","locale":"en"},"9383":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-405","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#context-and-compaction","content":"The conversation's model and effort","locale":"en"},"9384":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-406","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#context-and-compaction","content":"`window`, `window_source`","locale":"en"},"9385":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-407","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#context-and-compaction","content":"The model's window in tokens: from its listing (`catalog`), assumed (`default`), or what a station said in refusing a longer request (`learned`)","locale":"en"},"9386":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-408","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#context-and-compaction","content":"`limit`, `headroom`","locale":"en"},"9387":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-409","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#context-and-compaction","content":"Where the conversation is compacted, and the room kept for a reply","locale":"en"},"9388":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-410","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#context-and-compaction","content":"`used`, `used_source`","locale":"en"},"9389":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-411","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#context-and-compaction","content":"What the next request takes: as the station counted the last reply (`usage`), or estimated (`estimate`)","locale":"en"},"9390":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-412","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#context-and-compaction","content":"`last`, `totals`","locale":"en"},"9391":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-413","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#context-and-compaction","content":"Tokens of the last round counted, and of every reply on the path: `input`, `cached`, `output`, `reasoning`","locale":"en"},"9392":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-414","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#context-and-compaction","content":"`rounds`, `replies`, `compactions`, `last_compaction`","locale":"en"},"9393":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-415","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#context-and-compaction","content":"Counts on the path; the last compaction's `tokens_before`, `tokens_after`, `at`, `trigger`","locale":"en"},"9394":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-416","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#context-and-compaction","content":"`last_duration_ms`, `total_duration_ms`, `running_since`","locale":"en"},"9395":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-417","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#context-and-compaction","content":"How long replies worked; Unix seconds a reply has been running since, or `null`","locale":"en"},"9396":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-418","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#context-and-compaction","content":"`auto_compact`, `tools`, `approval`","locale":"en"},"9397":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-419","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#context-and-compaction","content":"`playground.auto_compact`, the tools on, the approval mode in effect","locale":"en"},"9398":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-420","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#context-and-compaction","content":"`POST /conversations/{id}/compact` compacts the conversation now, with an optional `instructions` (what the summary should pay attention to). It streams `checkpoint` (the checkpoint message as filed, its step `running`) and `done` (as kept). A `done` with `status` `error` means it failed and the conversation is as it was; closing the connection stops it the same way. It answers `409` while a reply is running and `400` when there is nothing to compact (no reply since the last compaction). Send the next question with the checkpoint's id as `parent_id`.","locale":"en"},"9399":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-421","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#context-and-compaction","content":"Replies compact the conversation by themselves (as they begin, between rounds of tool calls, and when the station refuses a round as too long); that shows as `compaction` events and a `compaction` step. From a compaction on, the model is sent a summary of everything before it, as a user message, with an acknowledgement after it; **Copy as API request** shows it.","locale":"en"},"9400":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-422","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#titles-branches-requests-and-the-session","content":"`POST /conversations/{id}/title` has a model name the conversation after its first exchange, and waits for it. The model is `playground.title_model`, else the conversation's own. A temporary conversation, one titled by a model already, and one with your own title are left as they are; if the model fails, the title stays. Answers the summary.","locale":"en"},"9401":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-423","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#titles-branches-requests-and-the-session","content":"`POST /conversations/{id}/branch` with `{\"message_id\": \"...\"}` creates a conversation holding the path up to that message, under new ids, with the same title, model, effort and approval mode, and `branched_from` set. Answers `201` with the full conversation.","locale":"en"},"9402":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-424","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#titles-branches-requests-and-the-session","content":"`GET /conversations/{id}/messages/{message_id}/request` returns the Chat Completions body behind a reply (or the one that would answer a question): `model`, `messages`, `stream: true`, `reasoning_effort` when set, and `tools` with `tool_choice` when tools are on. For a reply that used tools it is the first round. This is the Web UI's **Copy as API request**.","locale":"en"},"9403":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-425","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#titles-branches-requests-and-the-session","content":"`GET /session` returns `{\"conversation_id\": \"...\"}`, the conversation open last (`null` when none, or when it was temporary or deleted). `PUT /session` with the same body sets it (`null` for a new chat); an unknown id is a `400`. The Web UI reopens it on start.","locale":"en"},"9404":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-426","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#one-off-chat-and-the-model-list","content":"`POST /chat/completions` takes an OpenAI Chat Completions request (see OpenAI-compatible API) and answers like `/v1/chat/completions`, but with the tool access key instead of the model API key, and recorded in Usage under the `playground` origin. `playground.system_prompt` goes first unless the request has a `system` or `developer` message. Nothing is kept as a conversation.","locale":"en"},"9405":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-427","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#one-off-chat-and-the-model-list","content":"`GET /models` returns the same list as `GET /v1/models`.","locale":"en"},"9406":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-428","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground#one-off-chat-and-the-model-list","content":"Replies, titles and image descriptions made through conversations are recorded under the origins `playground`, `playground-title` and `playground-vision`.","locale":"en"},"9407":{"id":"/en/docs/api","page_id":"/en/docs/api","type":"page","content":"API overview","breadcrumbs":["Hoshimi Documentation","API reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/api","locale":"en"},"9408":{"id":"/en/docs/api-0","page_id":"/en/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api","content":"The whole of Hoshimi's HTTP interface: where the model, management and Playground APIs live and which key each uses, request checks and error shapes, streaming conventions, and the running server's /docs and /openapi.json.","locale":"en"},"9409":{"id":"/en/docs/api-1","page_id":"/en/docs/api","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/api#endpoint-groups","content":"Endpoint groups","locale":"en"},"9410":{"id":"/en/docs/api-2","page_id":"/en/docs/api","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/api#authentication","content":"Authentication","locale":"en"},"9411":{"id":"/en/docs/api-3","page_id":"/en/docs/api","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/api#request-checks","content":"Request checks","locale":"en"},"9412":{"id":"/en/docs/api-4","page_id":"/en/docs/api","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/api#error-shapes","content":"Error shapes","locale":"en"},"9413":{"id":"/en/docs/api-5","page_id":"/en/docs/api","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/api#streaming","content":"Streaming","locale":"en"},"9414":{"id":"/en/docs/api-6","page_id":"/en/docs/api","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/api#api-documentation-docs-and-openapijson","content":"API documentation: /docs and /openapi.json","locale":"en"},"9415":{"id":"/en/docs/api-7","page_id":"/en/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api","content":"Hoshimi's server offers three groups of endpoints next to the Web UI, at `http://127.0.0.1:10600` by default. This page covers the rules they share; each group's fields are on its own reference page.","locale":"en"},"9416":{"id":"/en/docs/api-8","page_id":"/en/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api#endpoint-groups","content":"Group","locale":"en"},"9417":{"id":"/en/docs/api-9","page_id":"/en/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api#endpoint-groups","content":"Paths","locale":"en"},"9418":{"id":"/en/docs/api-10","page_id":"/en/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api#endpoint-groups","content":"Key","locale":"en"},"9419":{"id":"/en/docs/api-11","page_id":"/en/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api#endpoint-groups","content":"Reference","locale":"en"},"9420":{"id":"/en/docs/api-12","page_id":"/en/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api#endpoint-groups","content":"OpenAI-compatible model API","locale":"en"},"9421":{"id":"/en/docs/api-13","page_id":"/en/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api#endpoint-groups","content":"`/v1/chat/completions`, `/v1/responses`, `/