g\"}`) every 15 seconds, only ever between complete events.","locale":"en"},"9568":{"id":"/en/docs/api-160","page_id":"/en/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api#api-documentation-docs-and-openapijson","content":"The running server has its own Swagger UI (`/docs`) and OpenAPI document (`/openapi.json`) listing every endpoint's fields; they are the authoritative reference. These pages explain usage; `/docs` describes structure.","locale":"en"},"9569":{"id":"/en/docs/api-161","page_id":"/en/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api#api-documentation-docs-and-openapijson","content":"With no tool access key set, the **Endpoints** section of **Overview** and **Settings** › **About** have an **API reference** button that opens `/docs`.","locale":"en"},"9570":{"id":"/en/docs/api-162","page_id":"/en/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api#api-documentation-docs-and-openapijson","content":"With a tool access key set, both addresses require it: opening them in a browser gives `401`, and the buttons are hidden. Fetch the OpenAPI document with the header:","locale":"en"},"9571":{"id":"/en/docs/api-163","page_id":"/en/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api#api-documentation-docs-and-openapijson","content":"The request bodies of `/v1/chat/completions`, `/v1/responses` and `/v1/messages` appear in OpenAPI as free-form objects; their fields are described in OpenAI-compatible API and Anthropic-compatible API.","locale":"en"},"9572":{"id":"/en/docs/api-164","page_id":"/en/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api#api-documentation-docs-and-openapijson","content":"<Card title=\"OpenAI-compatible API\" href=\"/docs/api-openai\" description=\"Chat Completions, Responses, the model list, routing, reasoning effort and classification.\" />","locale":"en"},"9573":{"id":"/en/docs/api-165","page_id":"/en/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api#api-documentation-docs-and-openapijson","content":"<Card title=\"Anthropic-compatible API\" href=\"/docs/api-anthropic\" description=\"Messages and token counting: native forwarding, conversion, thinking signatures, streaming and errors.\" />","locale":"en"},"9574":{"id":"/en/docs/api-166","page_id":"/en/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api#api-documentation-docs-and-openapijson","content":"<Card title=\"Management API\" href=\"/docs/api-management\" description=\"Every /api/v1 endpoint the Web UI uses.\" />","locale":"en"},"9575":{"id":"/en/docs/api-167","page_id":"/en/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api#api-documentation-docs-and-openapijson","content":"<Card title=\"Playground API\" href=\"/docs/api-playground\" description=\"Conversations, the event stream, tool approvals, steering, background commands and attachments.\" />","locale":"en"},"9576":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","type":"page","content":"Command reference","breadcrumbs":["Hoshimi Documentation","Command line"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli-commands","locale":"en"},"9577":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-0","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands","content":"Every hoshimi command: what it does, its arguments and options with their defaults, its output, the --json fields and examples, taken from each command's --help and the source.","locale":"en"},"9578":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-1","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#server","content":"Server","locale":"en"},"9579":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-2","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#serve","content":"`serve`","locale":"en"},"9580":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-3","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#checking-and-listing","content":"Checking and listing","locale":"en"},"9581":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-4","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","type":"