y requests do not keep cookies that responses set; each login has its own isolated cookie session. Hoshimi does not solve browser challenges (such as Cloudflare's) automatically and does not emulate TLS fingerprints.","locale":"en"},"10275":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-74","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#when-changes-apply","content":"After a save in the Web UI, new requests use the new route at once; streaming replies already running finish on their original connections. A network-only change does not rebuild a channel's account state: accounts held out of rotation and accounts marked as needing a login stay as they are. Changes made with `hoshimi config set` or by editing the file need a server restart. Environment variables are read on every request, but they are the ones the server process inherited when it started, so restart after changing them.","locale":"en"},"10276":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-75","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#network-diagnostics","content":"Each channel keeps the latest result of every kind of operation. On the **Channels** page, open a channel: its **Network** section lists the operations that failed most recently, with the error category and HTTP status; hover over an operation to see the target host and route.","locale":"en"},"10277":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-76","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#network-diagnostics","content":"The management API returns the same data:","locale":"en"},"10278":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-77","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#network-diagnostics","content":"A row holds only the operation, host, route source, time, status and error category: never request paths, query strings, headers, bodies, cookies or proxy URLs.","locale":"en"},"10279":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-78","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#network-diagnostics","content":"`operation` is one of: `catalog` (model catalogue), `inference`, `token_refresh`, `token_exchange`, `auth_start` (start authorization), `auth_poll` (authorization polling), `balance`, `checkin`, `request` (anything else).","locale":"en"},"10280":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-79","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#network-diagnostics","content":"`route` is one of: `direct`, `configured_proxy`, `environment_proxy`, `system_proxy` (Windows system proxy).","locale":"en"},"10281":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-80","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#network-diagnostics","content":"`kind` and what it means:","locale":"en"},"10282":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-81","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#network-diagnostics","content":"`kind`","locale":"en"},"10283":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-82","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#network-diagnostics","content":"Shown as","locale":"en"},"10284":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-83","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#network-diagnostics","content":"Meaning","locale":"en"},"10285":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-84","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#network-diagnostics","content":"`ok`","locale":"en"},"10286":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-85","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#network-diagnostics","content":"Success","locale":"en"},"10287":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-86","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#network-diagnostics","content":"The request succ