_id":"/en/docs/config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config#when-changes-take-effect","content":"`server.auto_refresh`, `server.auto_checkin`","locale":"en"},"10800":{"id":"/en/docs/config-288","page_id":"/en/docs/config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config#when-changes-take-effect","content":"See the note above","locale":"en"},"10801":{"id":"/en/docs/config-289","page_id":"/en/docs/config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config#when-changes-take-effect","content":"`playground.*`","locale":"en"},"10802":{"id":"/en/docs/config-290","page_id":"/en/docs/config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config#when-changes-take-effect","content":"From the next message","locale":"en"},"10803":{"id":"/en/docs/config-291","page_id":"/en/docs/config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config#when-changes-take-effect","content":"Changes made with `hoshimi config set` or by editing the file take effect after a server restart.","locale":"en"},"10804":{"id":"/en/docs/config-292","page_id":"/en/docs/config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config#reading-and-changing-it-from-the-command-line","content":"Keys are dotted. Values are parsed as JSON when they can be (numbers, `true`/`false`, lists, objects), otherwise kept as strings. `null` (or `none`) clears a value.","locale":"en"},"10805":{"id":"/en/docs/config-293","page_id":"/en/docs/config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config#reading-and-changing-it-from-the-command-line","content":"The whole configuration is validated before writing, so set keys that depend on each other in one go. To switch to proxy mode, for example, set the whole `network` object; `network.mode proxy` on its own is refused for lack of a proxy URL.","locale":"en"},"10806":{"id":"/en/docs/config-294","page_id":"/en/docs/config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config#reading-and-changing-it-from-the-command-line","content":"`show` and `get` print access keys, account credentials and proxy URLs as `***`. `get` reads what the file actually contains, and a key missing from the file gives `Unknown setting`.","locale":"en"},"10807":{"id":"/en/docs/config-295","page_id":"/en/docs/config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config#reading-and-changing-it-from-the-command-line","content":"Restart the server afterwards. The full command reference is in Commands.","locale":"en"},"10808":{"id":"/en/docs/config-296","page_id":"/en/docs/config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config#how-the-file-is-written","content":"Each save writes a temporary file in the same folder and then replaces `config.json` atomically, so a half-written file never appears. The file holds refresh tokens in plain text, so after each save its permissions are restricted to the owner (`0600`) where the file system supports that; Windows and some network mounts do not. Treat it as a credential store and do not share a filled-in copy.","locale":"en"},"10809":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","type":"page","content":"Architecture","breadcrumbs":["Hoshimi Documentation","Development"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-architecture","locale":"en"},"10810":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-0","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture","content":"The core / api / cli / webui layers and the layering rule, how Services is assembled and updated while running, the app factory, error mapping, and one model request from start to end.","locale":"en"},"10811":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-1","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#the-layering-rule","content":"The layering rule","locale":"en"},"10812":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-2","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#the-modules-of-core","content":"The modules of `core`","locale":"en"},"10813":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-3","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#services","content":"Services","locale":"en"},"10814":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-4","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#updating-the-configuration-while-running","content":"Updating the configuration while running","locale":"en"},"10815":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-5","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#the-app-factory","content":"The app factory","locale":"en"},"10816":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-6","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#errors","content":"Errors","locale":"en"},"10817":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-7","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#one-request-end-to-end","content":"One request, end to end","locale":"en"},"10818":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-8","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#middleware-and-route","content":"Middleware and route","locale":"en"},"10819":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-9","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#preparing-the-request","content":"Preparing the request","locale":"en"},"10820":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-10","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#counting-it","content":"Counting it","locale":"en"},"10821":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-11","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#routing-to-a-provider","content":"Routing to a provider","locale":"en"},"10822":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-12","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#account-rotation-and-the-upstream-protocol","content":"Account rotation and the upstream protocol","locale":"en"},"10823":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-13","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#the-public-protocol","content":"The public protocol","locale":"en"},"10824":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-14","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#the-command-line","content":"The command line","locale":"en"},"10825":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-15","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture","content":"Hoshimi's code has four layers, and dependencies run one way: `api` and `cli` depend on `core`; `core` depends on neither and imports no framework. Both entry points, the server and the command line, get the same `Services` from `build_services()` and wrap it in HTTP routes or commands of their own. This page covers the layering rule first, then `Services`, the app factory and errors, and finally follows one request all the way through.","locale":"en"},"10826":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-16","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#the-layering-rule","content":"Layer","locale":"en"},"10827":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-17","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#the-layering-rule","content":"May import","locale":"en"},"10828":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-18","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#the-layering-rule","content":"Must not import","locale":"en"},"10829":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-19","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#the-layering-rule","content":"`hoshimi/core`","locale":"en"},"10830":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-20","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#the-layering-rule","content":"The standard library, httpx, pydantic, cryptography and the optional cloud SDKs","locale":"en"},"10831":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-21","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#the-layering-rule","content":"`fastapi`, `starlette`, `typer`, `click`, `socketio`, `uvicorn`, `rich`; `hoshimi.api`, `hoshimi.cli`","locale":"en"},"10832":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-22","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#the-layering-rule","content":"`hoshimi/api`","locale":"en"},"10833":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-23","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#the-layering-rule","content":"`core`, FastAPI, Starlette","locale":"en"},"10834":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-24","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#the-layering-rule","content":"`hoshimi.cli`","locale":"en"},"10835":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-25","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#the-layering-rule","content":"`hoshimi/cli`","locale":"en"},"10836":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-26","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#the-layering-rule","content":"`core`, Typer, Rich; the `serve` command starts the `api` app","locale":"en"},"10837":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-27","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#the-layering-rule","content":"—","locale":"en"},"10838":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-28","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#the-layering-rule","content":"`hoshimi/webui`","locale":"en"},"10839":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-29","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#the-layering-rule","content":"Talks to the server over HTTP only","locale":"en"},"10840":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-30","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#the-layering-rule","content":"Python code","locale":"en"},"10841":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-31","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#the-layering-rule","content":"Two tests keep the rule:","locale":"en"},"10842":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-32","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#the-layering-rule","content":"`tests/core/test_architecture.py` parses the imports of every file under `hoshimi/core` and fails on any framework the table forbids; it also checks that no file there mentions `hoshimi.api` or `hoshimi.cli`. httpx is allowed, because the provider adapters are HTTP clients of their own upstream stations.","locale":"en"},"10843":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-33","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#the-layering-rule","content":"`tests/test_package_api.py` imports `hoshimi` in a fresh process and requires that neither `fastapi` nor `httpx` was loaded, and that the lazily exported `Services`, `build_services` and `create_app` are the very objects in the implementation modules.","locale":"en"},"10844":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-34","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#the-layering-rule","content":"What this buys: the domain logic can be tested and reused without a server, and the domain exceptions (`hoshimi/core/errors.py`) are mapped to HTTP responses by the API and to exit codes by the command line, while `core` stays out of it.","locale":"en"},"10845":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-35","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#the-modules-of-core","content":"Area","locale":"en"},"10846":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-36","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#the-modules-of-core","content":"Modules","locale":"en"},"10847":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-37","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#the-modules-of-core","content":"Assembly","locale":"en"},"10848":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-38","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#the-modules-of-core","content":"`context.py` (`Services`, `build_services`), `config.py` (`Settings`, reading and writing `config.json`), `paths.py` (the data folder)","locale":"en"},"10849":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-39","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture#the-modules-of-core","content":"Routing and providers","locale":"en"},"10850":{"id":"