lls in one direction (`.app-scroll` down, `.app-scroll-x` sideways, such as code blocks, tables and the stepper), so a sideways scrollbar anywhere else is a layout bug. The unit tests can only read the source; `scripts/check_layout.py` finds these bugs in real browsers.","locale":"en"},"11632":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-92","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#checking-the-layout-in-browsers-check_layoutpy","content":"Start a server first (`hoshimi serve` or `python scripts/dev.py dev`), ideally with a conversation in the Playground, so the chat list, the editor and the menus have something to open. The script:","locale":"en"},"11633":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-93","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#checking-the-layout-in-browsers-check_layoutpy","content":"opens `/overview`, `/models`, `/channels`, `/usage`, `/playground` and `/settings` in turn;","locale":"en"},"11634":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-94","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#checking-the-layout-in-browsers-check_layoutpy","content":"checks them in Chromium (with its scrollbars shown, as on a desktop) and Firefox (whose scrollbars float), at window widths of 320, 360, 600, 900, 1280 and 1600 pixels;","locale":"en"},"11635":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-95","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#checking-the-layout-in-browsers-check_layoutpy","content":"checks each page as it opens, then with its first menu open; on the Playground it also toggles the chat list and opens the message editor and the chat menu;","locale":"en"},"11636":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-96","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#checking-the-layout-in-browsers-check_layoutpy","cont