l`, `search_url`) are in Playground tools.","locale":"en"},"12643":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-188","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#a-system-prompt-for-the-playground","content":"The system prompt is empty by default, so a model gets only the conversation and the tool descriptions. The prompt below gives it the rest: when to act and when to ask, how to use the tools well, how to take approvals, steering and compaction, and how its reply is rendered here. Paste it into **Settings › General › Playground › System prompt**. It suits chats with and without tools, and any model; replies follow the language the user writes in.","locale":"en"},"12644":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-189","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#a-system-prompt-for-the-playground","content":"It is adapted from the base instructions OpenAI's Codex sends its models. What only Codex has is left out (its identity, its message channels, skills, apps, plugins and its JavaScript tool runner), and what the Playground does differently is fitted: local files are paths, not links; questions go in the reply; the tool descriptions already explain each tool, so the prompt says how to use them rather than what they are.","locale":"en"},"12645":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-190","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#a-system-prompt-for-the-playground","content":"Change it as you need: a line that names your project and its conventions, or one that sets the tone, goes at the end. The prompt only describes; what a tool may do is still decided by the tools you turn on and the approval mode (see Playground tools).","locale":"en"},"12646":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-191","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#where-chats-are-kept","content":"Chats, their messages and attachments live in `hoshimi.db` in the data folder (see Data folder and paths), and are kept until you delete them. The chat open last is remembered there too, which is how the Playground comes back to it from any browser. A reply cut off by a server stop is kept as stopped.","locale":"en"},"12647":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-192","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#where-chats-are-kept","content":"Every model call the Playground makes is recorded in Usage like any other call, under its own origin: `playground` for replies, `playground-title` for titles, `playground-vision` for image descriptions, `playground-compact` for compaction summaries and `playground-review` for automatic reviews of tool calls.","locale":"en"},"12648":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-193","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#where-chats-are-kept","content":"<Card title=\"Playground tools\" href=\"/docs/guide-agent\" description=\"Let a model read and edit files, run commands and search the web, with approvals.\" />","locale":"en"},"12649":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-194","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#where-chats-are-kept","content":"<Card title=\"Playground API\" href=\"/docs/api-playground\" description=\"The conversation routes and streamed events behind this page.\" />","locale":"en"},"12650":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","type":"page","content":"Settings","breadcrumbs":["Hoshimi Documentation","Web UI guides"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-settings","locale":"en"},"12651":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-0","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings","content":"The eight tabs of the Settings page: General, Tools, Access, Security, Network, Automation, Appearance and About, what each field does and the config key behind it.","locale":"en"},"12652":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-1","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#general","content":"General","locale":"en"},"12653":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-2","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#tools","content":"Tools","locale":"en"},"12654":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-3","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#access","content":"Access","locale":"en"},"12655":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-4","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#security","content":"Security","locale":"en"},"12656":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-5","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#network","content":"Network","locale":"en"},"12657":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-6","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#automation","content":"Automation","locale":"en"},"12658":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-7","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#appearance","content":"Appearance","locale":"en"},"12659":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-8","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#about","content":"About","locale":"en"},"12660":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-9","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#settings-that-are-not-in-the-interface","content":"Settings that are not in the interface","locale":"en"},"12661":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-10","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings","content":"**Settings** sits at the foot of the navigation and is split into eight tabs. The current tab is part of the address (such as `#/settings?tab=access`).","locale":"en"},"12662":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-11","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings","content":"Every field **saves on its own** as it changes; there is no overall save button. Switches and selections save at once, text and number fields when you leave them (or press Enter), and list fields each time a value is added or removed. A save shows **Saved**; a field that needs a restart shows **Saved · Takes effect after a restart.** An invalid value shows the reason and leaves the configuration unchanged.","locale":"en"},"12663":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-12","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings","content":"Apart from **Language** and **Appearance**, which are browser preferences, every setting is written to `config.json` in the data folder and applies to the running gateway at once. Each field below names its config key; the config file in full is described in Configuration file. Changes made from the command line or by editing the file need a server restart; changes made here do not (except the listening address and port).","locale":"en"},"12664":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-13","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings","content":"A channel's own switch and network route are not here but in that channel's details on the Channels page.","locale":"en"},"12665":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-14","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#general","content":"The **General** section:","locale":"en"},"12666":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-15","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#general","content":"Setting","locale":"en"},"12667":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-16","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#general","content":"Config key","locale":"en"},"12668":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-17","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#general","content":"What it does","locale":"en"},"12669":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-18","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#general","content":"**Language**","locale":"en"},"12670":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-19","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#general","content":"None (browser)","locale":"en"},"12671":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-20","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#general","content":"**Auto detect (system language)**, English, 简体中文, 日本語","locale":"en"},"12672":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-21","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#general","content":"**Default model**","locale":"en"},"12673":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-22","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#general","content":"`server.default_model`","locale":"en"},"12674":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-23","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#general","content":"Used when a request does not name a model. Searchable; **None** means a request must name its model","locale":"en"},"12675":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-24","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#general","content":"The **Requests** section, limits applied to every request the gateway accepts:","locale":"en"},"12676":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-25","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#general","content":"Setting","locale":"en"},"12677":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-26","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#general","