ccounts that declare it in `models` first, then accounts with no `models` declaration, then the rest.","locale":"en"},"13300":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-136","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#several-stations-in-one-channel","content":"With a single station you need no declarations. With several, use `models` to pin IDs to the right account, so a request does not land first on a station that does not know the ID.","locale":"en"},"13301":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-137","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#several-stations-in-one-channel","content":"Station rules (chat-model filters, free marks, capability tables) are matched by the `base_url` address, not the `preset` name: an account that says `preset: sambanova` but points `base_url` elsewhere does not get SambaNova's rules. A custom address gets no station rules at all.","locale":"en"},"13302":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-138","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#capability-declarations","content":"A station's `/models` usually carries IDs and nothing more. Without declarations, agg treats a model as text-only and non-thinking, and forwards the caller's request unchanged. Declare more in `options` when you need it:","locale":"en"},"13303":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-139","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#capability-declarations","content":"Key","locale":"en"},"13304":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-140","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#capability-declarations","content":"Meaning","locale":"en"},"13305":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-141","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#capability-declarations","content":"`vision`","locale":"en"},"13306":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-142","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#capability-declarations","content":"Whether the model accepts image input.","locale":"en"},"13307":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-143","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#capability-declarations","content":"`reasoning`","locale":"en"},"13308":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-144","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#capability-declarations","content":"Whether it is a thinking model.","locale":"en"},"13309":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-145","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#capability-declarations","content":"`context_window`","locale":"en"},"13310":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-146","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#capability-declarations","content":"Context length in tokens.","locale":"en"},"13311":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-147","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#capability-declarations","content":"`max_output`","locale":"en"},"13312":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-148","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#capability-declarations","content":"Maximum output length in tokens.","locale":"en"},"13313":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-149","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#capability-declarations","content":"`efforts`","locale":"en"},"13314":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-150","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#capability-declarations","content":"The thinking-level menu, in display order. Including `disabled` makes thinking switchable off.","locale":"en"},"13315":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-151","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#capability-declarations","content":"`effort_default`","locale":"en"},"13316":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-152","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#capability-declarations","content":"The default level.","locale":"en"},"13317":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-153","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#capability-declarations","content":"`effort_patch`","locale":"en"},"13318":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-154","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#capability-declarations","content":"JSON merged into the request body when a level is chosen; `\"$effort\"` inside it is replaced by the level's name.","locale":"en"},"13319":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-155","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#capability-declarations","content":"`effort_off_patch`","locale":"en"},"13320":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-156","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#capability-declarations","content":"JSON merged into the request body when the off level is chosen.","locale":"en"},"13321":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-157","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#capability-declarations","content":"`region_sensitive`","locale":"en"},"13322":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-158","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#capability-declarations","content":"Whether availability depends on the network exit's region.","locale":"en"},"13323":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-159","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#capability-declarations","content":"`model_specs`","locale":"en"},"13324":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-160","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#capability-declarations","content":"Per-model-ID overrides of the keys above.","locale":"en"},"13325":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-161","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#capability-declarations","content":"Precedence: account declarations outrank what the station's own listing says, which outranks the defaults; keys placed flat in `options` act as defaults, and the ID's `model_specs` entry is applied last. Flat keys apply to every ID in the channel, so when the channel holds several stations, put declarations in `model_specs`. For an undeclared ID, only two facts are filled in from models.dev, whether it thinks and whether it accepts images; context limits are never borrowed from another station. The same keys can also go in `providers.agg.options` as defaults for the whole channel. The full rules for capabilities and thinking levels are in Model behaviour.","locale":"en"},"13326":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-162","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#free-marks","content":"Each model's `free` field in `GET /v1/models` has three values: `true`, `false` and `null` (the station did not say). agg takes only what the station itself publishes:","locale":"en"},"13327":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-163","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#free-marks","content":"Read from the listing rows: `anyapi`, `gmi`, `opengateway`, `orcarouter`, `tokenrouter`, `xkiro`, `bai` (IDs with `:free`), `merge` (a route whose input and output prices are both 0).","locale":"en"},"13328":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-164","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#free-marks","content":"Fixed IDs recorded from the station's pricing page: `agnes`, `bai`, `commandcode`.","locale":"en"},"13329":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-165","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#free-marks","content":"`venice` and `llm7` are deliberately left unmarked: Venice's zero-priced models still require a positive account balance, and LLM7's prices are list prices, not a statement about an account's balance.","locale":"en"},"13330":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-166","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#free-marks","content":"A free mark describes the station's price list; it does not promise that an account has allowance or that a call will succeed.","locale":"en"},"13331":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-167","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#station-specific-handling","content":"**Chat-model filters**: listings from known stations drop image, video, embedding, transcription and other non-chat rows, with a filter written per station; a row missing the relevant fields is kept, so a station's schema change does not empty its catalogue. LLM7 is filtered on its own `model_type` field.","locale":"en"},"13332":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-168","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#station-specific-handling","content":"**CommandCode**: models whose name starts with `claude-` go to Anthropic Messages (`<base_url>/messages`); the station's vision and reasoning tables act as defaults, and account declarations win.","locale":"en"},"13333":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-169","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#station-specific-handling","content":"**Request shape**: requests to known stations turn `max_completion_tokens` into `max_tokens` and `developer` messages into `system`; requests to custom addresses are not rewritten. A station that answers a streaming request with one complete JSON document is still read correctly.","locale":"en"},"13334":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-170","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#station-specific-handling","content":"Most of these rules are ported from pi-free; the differences are in Migrating from pi-free.","locale":"en"},"13335":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","type":"page","content":"Anonymous lanes","breadcrumbs":["Hoshimi Documentation","Providers"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","locale":"en"},"13336":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-0","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","content":"The two free lanes that are on by default and need no account, OpenCode Zen and Kilo: what they offer, how to turn them off, how a key widens the catalogue, and how their protocols are handled.","locale":"en"},"13337":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-1","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#at-a-glance","content":"At a glance","locale":"en"},"13338":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-2","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#turning-the-anonymous-lanes-off","content":"Turning the anonymous lanes off","locale":"en"},"13339":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-3","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#opencode-zen-opencode","content":"OpenCode Zen (`opencode`)","locale":"en"},"13340":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-4","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#anonymous-use","content":"Anonymous use","locale":"en"},"13341":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-5","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#widening-the-catalogue-with-an-api-key","content":"Widening the catalogue with an API key","locale":"en"},"13342":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-6","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#protocol-handling","content":"Protocol handling","locale":"en"},"13343":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-7","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#thinking-levels","content":"Thinking levels","locale":"en"},"13344":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-8","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#region-and-probes","content":"Region and probes","locale":"en"},"13345":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-9","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#kilo-kilo","content":"Kilo (`kilo`)","locale":"en"},"13346":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-10","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#anonymous-use-1","content":"Anonymous use","locale":"en"},"13347":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-11","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#signing-in-with-a-key-or-a-device-code","content":"Signing in with a key or a device code","locale":"en"},"13348":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-12","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#request-handling-and-thinking-levels","content":"Request handling and thinking levels","locale":"en"},"13349":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-13","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#verification-scope","content":"Verification scope","locale":"en"},"13350":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-14","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","content":"On the first start, before there is any configuration, the `opencode` (OpenCode Zen) and `kilo` (Kilo AI) channels already work: each runs on a placeholder account with no credential in it and sends requests to the upstream's free models. On the **Channels** page both show **No account needed**.","locale":"en"},"13351":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-15","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","content":"Whether a model answers depends on the upstream's current models, quota and service state, and can differ by the region your network exits from. This page describes how the adapters work, not a promise about upstream availability.","locale":"en"},"13352":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-16","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#at-a-glance","content":"Channel","locale":"en"},"13353":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-17","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#at-a-glance","content":"Upstream","locale":"en"},"13354":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-18","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#at-a-glance","content":"Anonymous catalogue","locale":"en"},"13355":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-19","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#at-a-glance","content":"With an account","locale":"en"},"13356":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-20","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#at-a-glance","content":"`opencode`","locale":"en"},"13357":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-21","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#at-a-glance","content":"`https://opencode.ai/inference`","locale":"en"},"13358":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-22","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#at-a-glance","content":"The free slice of the live listing (IDs containing `free`, plus `big-pickle`, `space-bunny-free` and `union-alpha`)","locale":"en"},"13359":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-23","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#at-a-glance","content":"An API-key account uses its authenticated catalogue","locale":"en"},"13360":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-24","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#at-a-glance","content":"`kilo`","locale":"en"},"13361":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-25","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#at-a-glance","content":"`https://api.kilo.ai/api/gateway`","locale":"en"},"13362":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-26","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#at-a-glance","content":"Chat models the live listing marks `isFree: true`","locale":"en"},"13363":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-27","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#at-a-glance","content":"API key or device-code sign-in; the catalogue widens to every chat model the account can see","locale":"en"},"13364":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-28","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#at-a-glance","content":"To see the IDs available now:","locale":"en"},"13365":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-29","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#at-a-glance","content":"You can call them with the channel prefix, for example `opencode/big-pickle` or `kilo/kilo-auto/free`.","locale":"en"},"13366":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-30","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#turning-the-anonymous-lanes-off","content":"An anonymous lane is switched off only with `enabled: false` (with no accounts it is otherwise enabled automatically):","locale":"en"},"13367":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-31","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#turning-the-anonymous-lanes-off","content":"Or in `config.json`:","locale":"en"},"13368":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-32","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#turning-the-anonymous-lanes-off","content":"Switching the channel off on the **Channels** page does the same. To turn it back on, set `enabled` to `true` or delete the entry.","locale":"en"},"13369":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-33","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#anonymous-use","content":"Unless switched off, `opencode` runs on a placeholder account (`opencode-public`). The gateway reads the upstream `/v1/models` and keeps only the free slice: models whose ID has `free` as a separate segment (such as `mimo-v2.6-flash-free`), plus `big-pickle`, `space-bunny-free` and `union-alpha`, which are always treated as free. New free IDs keep the upstream's own spelling.","locale":"en"},"13370":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-34","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#anonymous-use","content":"The live listing is authoritative. A failed refresh keeps the last good catalogue; only a cold start with an unreachable listing uses the built-in historical fallback list.","locale":"en"},"13371":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-35","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#widening-the-catalogue-with-an-api-key","content":"On **Channels** › **OpenCode Zen**, click **Add account** and choose **API key**, or write it into `config.json`:","locale":"en"},"13372":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-36","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#widening-the-catalogue-with-an-api-key","content":"Once the channel has accounts, it uses only the ones you configured; the anonymous placeholder is no longer added. An account without `api_key` sends its requests anonymously.","locale":"en"},"13373":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-37","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#widening-the-catalogue-with-an-api-key","content":"When the first account has a key, the catalogue is no longer cut down to the free slice; the key's own permissions still apply.","locale":"en"},"13374":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-38","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#widening-the-catalogue-with-an-api-key","content":"`project_id` is sent as the `x-opencode-project` header; the default is `global`.","locale":"en"},"13375":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-39","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#widening-the-catalogue-with-an-api-key","content":"The OpenCode Go plan is a separate channel, `opencode-go`; see Local and compatible endpoints.","locale":"en"},"13376":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-40","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#protocol-handling","content":"The anonymous lane implements the v2 protocol after the external dsh-our-free-model project's `src/upstream.js` (snapshot `f0b979f`). The snapshot identifies the porting baseline, not a recent test against the upstream.","locale":"en"},"13377":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-41","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#protocol-handling","content":"Requests go to endpoints under `/inference/v1` with `User-Agent: opencode/latest/2.0.26/cli` and `x-opencode-client: cli`; the legacy `x-opencode-request` is not sent.","locale":"en"},"13378":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-42","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#protocol-handling","content":"The `x-opencode-session`, `x-opencode-session-id`, `x-session-affinity` and `x-session-id` headers carry the same session ID. It is derived per account and conversation (descending encoding) from the body's `session_id`, `conversation_id` or `user`, in that order, or else from the first user message. Send a different `session_id` for separate conversations that open with the same message.","locale":"en"},"13379":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-43","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#protocol-handling","content":"The endpoint follows the model: `muse-spark-*` uses `/v1/responses`, `union-alpha` uses `/v1/messages`, everything else `/v1/chat/completions`.","locale":"en"},"13380":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-44","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#protocol-handling","content":"Anonymous requests declare the reference implementation's `read` and `shell` tool definitions (the upstream compares tool descriptions). A caller tool with the same name but a different definition is sent under an alias (such as `read_client`), consistently in declarations, history and forced choices, and restored in the response.","locale":"en"},"13381":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-45","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#protocol-handling","content":"The caller cannot actually run those two injected tools. When the model calls only tools the caller did not offer, the gateway answers it with `unsupported call: <name>` and asks again in the same session, for at most two rounds; if the model keeps calling them, the request fails with a 502 error. The caller sees only the text and calls to its own tools.","locale":"en"},"13382":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-46","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#protocol-handling","content":"When the caller sets `tool_choice: \"none\"`, the field is left out of the upstream request and the gateway makes sure no tool call reaches the caller.","locale":"en"},"13383":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-47","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#protocol-handling","content":"Accounts with an API key skip all of this tool handling; the caller's tools are sent as declared.","locale":"en"},"13384":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-48","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#thinking-levels","content":"These IDs use the thinking menus declared by the reference implementation; other IDs follow the shared capability table (see Model behaviour).","locale":"en"},"13385":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-49","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#thinking-levels","content":"Model","locale":"en"},"13386":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-50","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#thinking-levels","content":"Levels","locale":"en"},"13387":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-51","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#thinking-levels","content":"Default","locale":"en"},"13388":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-52","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#thinking-levels","content":"Thinking can be switched off","locale":"en"},"13389":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-53","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#thinking-levels","content":"`deepseek-v4.1-flash-free`","locale":"en"},"13390":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-54","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#thinking-levels","content":"`disabled`, `low`, `high`, `max`","locale":"en"},"13391":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-55","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#thinking-levels","content":"`high`","locale":"en"},"13392":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-56","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#thinking-levels","content":"Yes","locale":"en"},"13393":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-57","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#thinking-levels","content":"`glm-5.3-flash-free`","locale":"en"},"13394":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-58","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#thinking-levels","content":"`low`, `high`, `max`","locale":"en"},"13395":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-59","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#thinking-levels","content":"`high`","locale":"en"},"13396":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-60","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#thinking-levels","content":"No","locale":"en"},"13397":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-61","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#thinking-levels","content":"`nemotron-3.5-super-vl-free`","locale":"en"},"13398":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-62","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#thinking-levels","content":"`disabled`, `minimal`, `low`, `medium`, `high`, `xhigh`","locale":"en"},"13399":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-63","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#thinking-levels","content":"`high`","locale":"en"},"13400":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-64","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#thinking-levels","content":"Yes","locale":"en"},"13401":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-65","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#thinking-levels","content":"`space-bunny-free`","locale":"en"},"13402":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-66","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#thinking-levels","content":"`low`, `medium`, `high`, `xhigh`, `max`","locale":"en"},"13403":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-67","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#thinking-levels","content":"`high`","locale":"en"},"13404":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-68","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#thinking-levels","content":"No","locale":"en"},"13405":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-69","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#thinking-levels","content":"The level is sent in the `reasoning_effort` field.","locale":"en"},"13406":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-70","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#region-and-probes","content":"The listing names IDs only; it cannot say whether your network exit may use a given model, and the `muse-spark` family is marked as region-sensitive. `opencode` takes part in the default availability probe, so you can confirm with one real request from the **Models** page or `POST /api/v1/probe`; see Model behaviour.","locale":"en"},"13407":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-71","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#anonymous-use-1","content":"Unless switched off, `kilo` runs on a placeholder account (`kilo-public`) and calls the Kilo gateway with no credential. The catalogue keeps only the chat models the upstream marks `isFree: true` (embedding, image, audio and similar rows are excluded); paid IDs only answer 401 without a key. A cold start with an unreachable listing uses the built-in historical fallback list (such as `kilo-auto/free` and `openrouter/free`).","locale":"en"},"13408":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-72","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#anonymous-use-1","content":"The anonymous free pool is protected by no credential at all, and the upstreams behind the free models may log prompts. Do not send sensitive content through it.","locale":"en"},"13409":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-73","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#signing-in-with-a-key-or-a-device-code","content":"There are two ways to add a Kilo account:","locale":"en"},"13410":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-74","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#signing-in-with-a-key-or-a-device-code","content":"The terminal prints a verification link and a code (in the Web UI, click **Sign in**; the dialog shows the **Verification code**). Confirm in the browser and the account is written to `config.json`. Kilo returns a long-lived key, not a renewable OAuth token, so it is never renewed on a timer.","locale":"en"},"13411":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-75","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#signing-in-with-a-key-or-a-device-code","content":"You can also paste an API key in **Add account**, or write it into `config.json`:","locale":"en"},"13412":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-76","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#signing-in-with-a-key-or-a-device-code","content":"The account accepts any one of `api_key`, `access_token` or `token`.","locale":"en"},"13413":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-77","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#signing-in-with-a-key-or-a-device-code","content":"With a credentialed account, the catalogue includes every chat model the account can see; `options.free_only: true` keeps it to free models.","locale":"en"},"13414":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-78","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#signing-in-with-a-key-or-a-device-code","content":"As with `opencode`, once the channel has accounts the anonymous placeholder is no longer added; an account with no credential calls anonymously.","locale":"en"},"13415":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-79","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#request-handling-and-thinking-levels","content":"Requests use OpenAI Chat Completions: `max_completion_tokens` becomes `max_tokens`, `developer` messages become `system`, `strict` is removed from tool definitions, and `store` and `reasoning_effort` are dropped.","locale":"en"},"13416":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-80","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#request-handling-and-thinking-levels","content":"Thinking levels come from the capabilities each listing row declares and are sent as `reasoning: {\"effort\": ...}`; switching thinking off sends `reasoning: {\"enabled\": false}`.","locale":"en"},"13417":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-81","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#request-handling-and-thinking-levels","content":"Models under `stepfun/`, `liquid/` and `thinkingmachines/` require thinking, and `kilo-auto/free` and `openrouter/free` accept the parameter but keep thinking, so their menus have no off level.","locale":"en"},"13418":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-82","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#request-handling-and-thinking-levels","content":"Kilo is not part of the default availability probe: the anonymous listing is already the free pool's verdict.","locale":"en"},"13419":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-83","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#verification-scope","content":"`tests/core/test_opencode_lane.py`, `tests/core/test_pi_free_parity.py` and the protocol tests cover local regressions; they do not replace a successful request from a particular network exit. Model availability, regional limits and quota are settled by the upstream's current answers or an explicit probe.","locale":"en"},"13420":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","type":"page","content":"Cloud platforms","breadcrumbs":["Hoshimi Documentation","Providers"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","locale":"en"},"13421":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-0","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","content":"Connect Azure OpenAI, Cloudflare Workers AI and AI Gateway, the Gemini Developer API, Vertex AI and Amazon Bedrock, plus the two special protocols Radius and TypeSafe: credentials, account fields, protocol selection and limits.","locale":"en"},"13422":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-1","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#optional-dependencies","content":"Optional dependencies","locale":"en"},"13423":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-2","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#azure-openai-azure","content":"Azure OpenAI (`azure`)","locale":"en"},"13424":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-3","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#cloudflare-cloudflare-workers-ai-cloudflare-ai-gateway","content":"Cloudflare (`cloudflare-workers-ai`, `cloudflare-ai-gateway`)","locale":"en"},"13425":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-4","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#gemini-developer-api-google","content":"Gemini Developer API (`google`)","locale":"en"},"13426":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-5","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#google-vertex-ai-google-vertex","content":"Google Vertex AI (`google-vertex`)","locale":"en"},"13427":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-6","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#amazon-bedrock-amazon-bedrock","content":"Amazon Bedrock (`amazon-bedrock`)","locale":"en"},"13428":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-7","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#radius-radius","content":"Radius (`radius`)","locale":"en"},"13429":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-8","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#typesafe-typesafe","content":"TypeSafe (`typesafe`)","locale":"en"},"13430":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-9","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#protocol-selection","content":"Protocol selection","locale":"en"},"13431":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-10","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","content":"Every channel on this page needs your own cloud account. Pick the channel ID that matches the upstream endpoint, protocol, credentials and plan; a similar model name does not make credentials interchangeable. For example, `gemini` is Code Assist (see Free stations), `google` is the Gemini Developer API and `google-vertex` is Vertex AI; `amazon-bedrock` and `bedrock-mantle` are two services configured separately.","locale":"en"},"13432":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-11","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","content":"The JSON below are fragments of `providers` in the data folder's `config.json`, not files to place next to the program. Replace the placeholders and enable only the channels you use; restart after editing the file. **Add account** under **Channels** takes effect immediately, and its form lists the fields for each **Authentication method**.","locale":"en"},"13433":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-12","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#optional-dependencies","content":"Vertex default credentials and service accounts need Google's auth library; Bedrock needs the AWS SDK:","locale":"en"},"13434":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-13","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#optional-dependencies","content":"Vertex API-key mode and ordinary HTTP channels need neither. A missing dependency or credential produces a clear error; it never falls back to anonymous access.","locale":"en"},"13435":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-14","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#azure-openai-azure","content":"Give the Azure resource name, the key, the public model IDs and the deployment mapping:","locale":"en"},"13436":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-15","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#azure-openai-azure","content":"Field","locale":"en"},"13437":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-16","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#azure-openai-azure","content":"Meaning","locale":"en"},"13438":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-17","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#azure-openai-azure","content":"`resource`","locale":"en"},"13439":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-18","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#azure-openai-azure","content":"The resource name; the default root is `https://<resource>.openai.azure.com/openai/v1`.","locale":"en"},"13440":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-19","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#azure-openai-azure","content":"`base_url`","locale":"en"},"13441":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-20","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#azure-openai-azure","content":"Optional; replaces the address built from `resource`.","locale":"en"},"13442":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-21","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#azure-openai-azure","content":"`api_key`","locale":"en"},"13443":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-22","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#azure-openai-azure","content":"Sent in the `api-key` header.","locale":"en"},"13444":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-23","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#azure-openai-azure","content":"`models`","locale":"en"},"13445":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-24","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#azure-openai-azure","content":"The public model IDs (required in the Web UI form).","locale":"en"},"13446":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-25","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#azure-openai-azure","content":"`deployments`","locale":"en"},"13447":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-26","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#azure-openai-azure","content":"Maps model IDs to deployment names. The upstream request's `model` becomes the deployment name, while capabilities and protocol are still looked up by the public ID.","locale":"en"},"13448":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-27","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#azure-openai-azure","content":"`protocol`","locale":"en"},"13449":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-28","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#azure-openai-azure","content":"Responses by default; `\"chat\"` selects Chat Completions.","locale":"en"},"13450":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-29","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#cloudflare-cloudflare-workers-ai-cloudflare-ai-gateway","content":"Workers AI needs an account ID; AI Gateway also needs a gateway ID:","locale":"en"},"13451":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-30","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#cloudflare-cloudflare-workers-ai-cloudflare-ai-gateway","content":"**Workers AI**: the address is `https://api.cloudflare.com/client/v4/accounts/<account_id>/ai/v1`. The catalogue comes from Cloudflare's native model search, keeping text-generation tasks only; `models` declared on the account replaces it.","locale":"en"},"13452":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-31","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#cloudflare-cloudflare-workers-ai-cloudflare-ai-gateway","content":"**AI Gateway**: Chat requests go to `https://gateway.ai.cloudflare.com/v1/<account_id>/<gateway_id>/compat` with the key in the `cf-aig-authorization` header. The Messages protocol uses the gateway's `/anthropic/v1/messages` instead, and Responses uses `/openai/responses`.","locale":"en"},"13453":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-32","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#cloudflare-cloudflare-workers-ai-cloudflare-ai-gateway","content":"Both accept `base_url` in place of the built address. Set `protocol` or `model_protocols` (see the end of this page) only for a protocol the upstream really supports.","locale":"en"},"13454":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-33","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#gemini-developer-api-google","content":"The default is native Gemini streaming (`generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta`) with the key in `x-goog-api-key`. `protocol: \"chat\"` switches to Google's OpenAI-compatible Chat endpoint.","locale":"en"},"13455":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-34","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#gemini-developer-api-google","content":"The catalogue is the native model list (paginated), keeping models that support `generateContent`; `models` can declare it instead.","locale":"en"},"13456":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-35","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#gemini-developer-api-google","content":"The native translation keeps function calls and their opaque thought signatures, so multi-turn tool use replays correctly.","locale":"en"},"13457":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-36","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#gemini-developer-api-google","content":"Thinking is set with `reasoning_effort`, or with Google's own `thinking_config` (not both at once).","locale":"en"},"13458":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-37","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#gemini-developer-api-google","content":"This channel does not use the Code Assist sign-in of the `gemini` channel.","locale":"en"},"13459":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-38","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#google-vertex-ai-google-vertex","content":"Use one of three authentication methods: an API key, application default credentials (ADC), or a service-account file.","locale":"en"},"13460":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-39","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#google-vertex-ai-google-vertex","content":"Authentication method","locale":"en"},"13461":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-40","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#google-vertex-ai-google-vertex","content":"Account fields","locale":"en"},"13462":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-41","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#google-vertex-ai-google-vertex","content":"**API key**","locale":"en"},"13463":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-42","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#google-vertex-ai-google-vertex","content":"`api_key`; optional `project`, `location`","locale":"en"},"13464":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-43","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#google-vertex-ai-google-vertex","content":"**Google default credentials**","locale":"en"},"13465":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-44","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#google-vertex-ai-google-vertex","content":"`auth: \"adc\"`, `project` (required), optional `location`","locale":"en"},"13466":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-45","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#google-vertex-ai-google-vertex","content":"**Google service account file**","locale":"en"},"13467":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-46","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#google-vertex-ai-google-vertex","content":"`service_account_file` (a path on the server), `project` (required), optional `location`","locale":"en"},"13468":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-47","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#google-vertex-ai-google-vertex","content":"ADC and service accounts need `hoshimi[google]`, and the credentials must be visible to the process running Hoshimi. Missing or expired credentials are reported as an error; there is no silent switch to another method.","locale":"en"},"13469":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-48","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#google-vertex-ai-google-vertex","content":"`location` defaults to `global`; a region name (such as `us-central1`) selects the regional endpoint.","locale":"en"},"13470":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-49","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#google-vertex-ai-google-vertex","content":"The default is the native Gemini protocol; `protocol: \"chat\"` connects to Vertex's OpenAI-compatible endpoint, which requires `project`.","locale":"en"},"13471":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-50","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#google-vertex-ai-google-vertex","content":"The catalogue comes from Google's publisher model list; the models your account is authorised for can be declared with `models` instead.","locale":"en"},"13472":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-51","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#amazon-bedrock-amazon-bedrock","content":"Uses Bedrock ConverseStream. Every authentication method needs `hoshimi[bedrock]`.","locale":"en"},"13473":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-52","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#amazon-bedrock-amazon-bedrock","content":"Authentication method","locale":"en"},"13474":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-53","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#amazon-bedrock-amazon-bedrock","content":"Account fields","locale":"en"},"13475":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-54","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#amazon-bedrock-amazon-bedrock","content":"**AWS default credentials**","locale":"en"},"13476":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-55","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#amazon-bedrock-amazon-bedrock","content":"`auth: \"aws\"`, using the AWS credential chain","locale":"en"},"13477":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-56","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#amazon-bedrock-amazon-bedrock","content":"**AWS profile**","locale":"en"},"13478":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-57","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#amazon-bedrock-amazon-bedrock","content":"`profile`","locale":"en"},"13479":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-58","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#amazon-bedrock-amazon-bedrock","content":"**AWS access keys**","locale":"en"},"13480":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-59","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#amazon-bedrock-amazon-bedrock","content":"`aws_access_key_id`, `aws_secret_access_key`, optional `aws_session_token`","locale":"en"},"13481":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-60","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#amazon-bedrock-amazon-bedrock","content":"**API key**","locale":"en"},"13482":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-61","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#amazon-bedrock-amazon-bedrock","content":"`api_key` (a Bedrock bearer key); `models` is required","locale":"en"},"13483":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-62","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#amazon-bedrock-amazon-bedrock","content":"`region` defaults to `us-east-1`. In bearer mode, `base_url` can replace `https://bedrock-runtime.<region>.amazonaws.com`.","locale":"en"},"13484":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-63","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#amazon-bedrock-amazon-bedrock","content":"SDK modes can list the text foundation models that support streaming; a bearer key is not authorised for the control-plane model listing, so declare `models`. Account-specific inference profile IDs or ARNs should also be declared explicitly.","locale":"en"},"13485":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-64","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#amazon-bedrock-amazon-bedrock","content":"The adapter translates messages, supported images, tool calls and results, usage and thinking signatures; a `thinking` object in the request body is passed upstream as an additional model field. Not every Bedrock model supports every feature, and model access is still decided by your AWS account.","locale":"en"},"13486":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-65","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#amazon-bedrock-amazon-bedrock","content":"`bedrock-mantle` is another service: Bedrock's OpenAI-compatible endpoint, configured separately with a bearer key and its own address (default `https://bedrock-mantle.us-east-1.api.aws/v1`):","locale":"en"},"13487":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-66","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#radius-radius","content":"Radius uses a dedicated pi-messages protocol rather than a generic Chat endpoint.","locale":"en"},"13488":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-67","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#radius-radius","content":"**Adding an account**: `hoshimi login radius` (device-code sign-in, renewable token), or an API key in **Add account**.","locale":"en"},"13489":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-68","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#radius-radius","content":"**Models**: the inference address and model list are read from the gateway's `/v1/config`. The account's `gateway` field replaces the default gateway `https://radius.pi.dev`.","locale":"en"},"13490":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-69","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#typesafe-typesafe","content":"TypeSafe is a classification service, not a chat model: its models do not appear in `/v1/models` and cannot be used for chat.","locale":"en"},"13491":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-70","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#typesafe-typesafe","content":"`classifiers` is optional and defaults to `[\"jev-latest\"]`. `GET /v1/classifiers` lists the available classifiers, and classification requests go to `POST /v1/classify`:","locale":"en"},"13492":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-71","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#typesafe-typesafe","content":"`model` comes from `/v1/classifiers`, in the form `typesafe/<classifier>`.","locale":"en"},"13493":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-72","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#typesafe-typesafe","content":"`state` is an object and `questions` a non-empty object; their contents are passed to TypeSafe as they are.","locale":"en"},"13494":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-73","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#typesafe-typesafe","content":"Each question's `type` is `bool`, `score` or `choice`. `bool` returns a probability; `score` and `choice` return a score or a choice with its confidence.","locale":"en"},"13495":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-74","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#typesafe-typesafe","content":"Image input is not supported. The full field definitions are in the running server's `/docs`.","locale":"en"},"13496":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-75","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#protocol-selection","content":"Channels such as `azure` and `cloudflare-ai-gateway` speak several protocols. The protocol for a model is decided in this order:","locale":"en"},"13497":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-76","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#protocol-selection","content":"The protocol named for the model in the channel option `options.model_protocols`, for example `{\"claude-sonnet\": \"messages\"}`.","locale":"en"},"13498":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-77","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#protocol-selection","content":"The account's `protocol` field.","locale":"en"},"13499":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-78","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#protocol-selection","content":"Protocol information carried by the model's catalogue row.","locale":"en"},"13500":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-79","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#protocol-selection","content":"The channel's default protocol.","locale":"en"},"13501":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-80","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#protocol-selection","content":"The values are `chat`, `responses` and `messages`, with the aliases `openai-completions`, `openai-responses` and `anthropic-messages` also accepted. `google` and `google-vertex` use `gemini` or `chat`. Set these only for protocols the upstream really supports. More protocol-related options are in Local and compatible endpoints.","locale":"en"},"13502":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-81","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#protocol-selection","content":"Availability has to be confirmed with a real request from a configured account; this page describes the configuration behaviour that is implemented. The full service mapping is in the provider inventory.","locale":"en"},"13503":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-inventory","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-inventory","type":"page","content":"Provider inventory","breadcrumbs":["Hoshimi Documentation","Providers"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-inventory","locale":"en"},"13504":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-inventory-0","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-inventory","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-inventory","content":"Where each provider definition comes from, its endpoint and protocol, how it authenticates, and how far Hoshimi covers it. Generated.","locale":"en"},"13505":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-inventory-1","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-inventory","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-inventory","content":"Source snapshots: pi `482c1381a`, pi-free `2da9909`, free-claude-code `f919f46d` (2026-10-19).","locale":"en"},"13506":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-inventory-2","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-inventory","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-inventory","content":"This page is generated by `scripts/generate_provider_inventory.py` from `hoshimi/core/provider_sources.py`; do not edit it by hand. Reference repositories are not runtime dependencies.","locale":"en"},"13507":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-inventory-3","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-inventory","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-inventory","content":"Deduplication uses endpoint + protocol + credential types + plan. Existing native lanes and all 22 agg presets are retained.","locale":"en"},"13508":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-inventory-4","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-inventory","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-inventory","content":"`native` and `agg` record an existing entry point, not live endpoint verification or complete upstream parity. `partial` has protocol gaps; `planned` is not registered yet.","locale":"en"},"13509":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-inventory-5","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-inventory","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-inventory","content":"MiniMax API uses `minimax-api` to preserve the Agent service. Gemini Developer API uses `google`, separate from Code Assist `gemini`. The legacy `openai-codex` source maps to the existing `codex` account namespace. TypeSafe is classification, not chat.","locale":"en"},"13510":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-inventory-6","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-inventory","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-inventory","content":"Source snapshots and coverage labels do not establish current live availability. See Providers for registration, plans and authentication.","locale":"en"},"13511":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-inventory-7","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-inventory","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-inventory","content":"Source","locale":"en"},"13512":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-inventory-8","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-inventory","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-inventory","content":"Source ID","locale":"en"},"13513":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-inventory-9","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-inventory","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-inventory","content":"Hoshimi ID","locale":"en"},"13514":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-inventory-10","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-inventory","