milar model name does not make credentials interchangeable. For example, `gemini` is Code Assist (see Free stations), `google` is the Gemini Developer API and `google-vertex` is Vertex AI; `amazon-bedrock` and `bedrock-mantle` are two services configured separately."],[8340,"Every channel's usage is first normalized to OpenAI's fields, then recorded:"],[11085,"Every chunk `stream_raw` yields is a dictionary with a `type` key. Whether the upstream speaks OpenAI Chat, Anthropic Messages, Gemini or TRAE SOLO, the adapter turns it into these:"],[12570,"Every code block, diagram and SVG has a toolbar for a head: an icon for what it holds (code, a command, a diff, a diagram, an image, a page), its language (**Python**, **Bash**…, or **Text** when the block names none), and its buttons, with **Copy code** last. HTML written directly in a reply (outside a code block) is shown as text."],[12064,"Every command (`shell`, `exec_command`, and `write_stdin` when it types), every file change, and reading anything outside the workspace"],[9595,"Every command takes these two options; the tables leave them out:"],[9773,"Every command, `serve` included, reads both."],[12871,"Every config key is in Configuration file."],[9125,"Every conversation uses the tools `playground.tools` turns on; a conversation has no tools of its own. (`tools_on` and `tools_off`, which older clients send, are ignored.)"],[8404,"Every counter, chart and call record is cleared; this cannot be undone. Calls in flight are still recorded when they end."],[8674,"Every date with usage"],[9753,"Every environment variable Hoshimi reads: its own HOSHIMI_DATA_DIR and HOSHIMI_LOG_LEVEL, the standard variables behind the default data folder and proxies, the credential variables the cloud SDKs read, the variables set for the Playground's commands, and the ones it deliberately ignores."],[8581,"Every error uses Anthropic's shape:"],[12662,"Every field **saves on its own** as it changes; there is no overall save button. Switches and selections save at once, text and number fields when you leave them (or press Enter), and list fields each time a value is added or removed. A save shows **Saved**; a field that needs a restart shows **Saved · Takes effect after a restart.** An invalid value shows the reason and leaves the configuration unchanged."],[9577,"Every hoshimi command: what it does, its arguments and options with their defaults, its output, the --json fields and examples, taken from each command's --help and the source."],[11540,"Every kind of check in Hoshimi: the pytest layout and shared fixtures, how provider and route tests are written, the Web UI's Vitest rule tests, the generated-type check, check_layout.py for sideways overflow in real browsers, and how CI runs them."],[8148,"Every log line (written to stderr; there is no log file). `HOSHIMI_LOG_LEVEL=DEBUG hoshimi serve` or `hoshimi serve --debug` adds detail"],[12647,"Every model call the Playground makes is recorded in Usage like any other call, under its own origin: `playground` for replies, `playground-title` for titles, `playground-vision` for image descriptions, `playground-compact` for compaction summaries and `playground-review` for automatic reviews of tool calls."],[12587,"Every model has a **context window**: how much of a conversation it can read at once. The ring beside the send button shows how much of it is left; press it, or type `/status`, for the details. The window is the one the model's station lists. When a station refuses a request as too long and names its real limit, that limit is used from then on."],[13020,"Every model you can call: search, abilities, context length, availability probes, and a shortcut to try one in the Playground"],[9445,"Every other path"],[11790,"Every page's root, the `.body` of `AppDialog` and `SideSheet`, and `DataTable`'s `.row` use `var(--app-scroll-lane)` in `padding-inline-end`"],[11005,"Every provider (a \"channel\" in the Web UI) is a `Provider` subclass in `hoshimi/core/providers/`: it holds the provider's accounts and options, knows how to send one turn upstream with one account, and turns the upstream stream into **normalized chunks**. The shared parts, account rotation, retries, cooldowns and the catalogue cache, live in the base class; an adapter writes only what is particular to its station."],[8402,"Every record has a sequence number `seq` that never repeats, even after the statistics are cleared, so it is safe as a paging cursor."],[10465,"Every request (WebSockets included) goes through these four checks in order. The first failure answers the request at once; nothing reaches upstream:"],[10210,"Every request Hoshimi sends upstream (model catalogues, inference, login, token refresh, balances, check-in) picks its route from a network policy: direct, or through a proxy. There is one global default and each channel can override it. This page shows how to write these policies, when they apply, and where to look when something fails."],[9467,"Every request passes these checks, in this order, before it reaches an endpoint. A request that fails one gets:"],[10744,"Every save (Web UI, API, `hoshimi config set`) and every start (`hoshimi serve`, `hoshimi check`) validates the whole configuration first; when it fails, the file is left as it was. The possible errors:"],[11631,"Every scrolling area in the Web UI scrolls in one direction (`.app-scroll` down, `.app-scroll-x` sideways, such as code blocks, tables and the stepper), so a sideways scrollbar anywhere else is a layout bug. The unit tests can only read the source; `scripts/check_layout.py` finds these bugs in real browsers."],[11781,"Every scrolling area scrolls through `.app-scroll`; see below"],[10894,"Every service that holds the settings object (renewal, check-in, login, update checks, the network client) is pointed at the new one, so none of them later writes the old configuration back over the file."],[10363,"Every setting and the channel accounts' credentials"],[11507