ame the conversation"],[12875,"Headline tiles"],[12273,"Held out of rotation for a while, **Rate limited** or **Blocked by policy**; it returns by itself"],[12083,"High"],[12087,"High and critical are things like deleting data that can't be recovered, force-pushing shared branches, sending secrets or private data somewhere untrusted, reading credentials from unusual places, or weakening security for good."],[8213,"Holds live in memory and a restart clears them, but that does not lift the upstream's limit."],[7850,"Holds live in memory and a restart clears them. But a hold usually follows an upstream rate limit (lasting as long as the upstream said, one hour when it said nothing) or a policy block (30 minutes); a restart does not lift the upstream's limit, and the account will soon be held again."],[8019,"Holds the account for 30 minutes without renewing its token, then the next account"],[8016,"Holds this account out of rotation, then the next account"],[378,"Hoshimi"],[5323,"Hoshimi"],[8117,"Hoshimi"],[13060,"Hoshimi"],[14782,"Hoshimi adjusts requests for each service's known differences, for example:"],[9942,"Hoshimi decides per request, from the account that will serve it:"],[14711,"Hoshimi does not scan local ports: it contacts these addresses only after you add an account and the channel is enabled."],[8452,"Hoshimi finds the provider through model routing, then looks at the accounts of that provider that can serve the model:"],[10131,"Hoshimi has two independent keys, and a client uses only one of them:"],[10439,"Hoshimi holds the credentials of your upstream accounts: whoever can reach it can spend them. The default configuration listens on `127.0.0.1` only and sets no keys, which suits a computer only you use. When other programs or other machines need access, set keys and access limits as described here."],[5776,"Hoshimi ID"],[13513,"Hoshimi ID"],[13065,"Hoshimi is a model gateway written in Python. It puts free model stations (Cline, TRAE, ZCode, Qoder, MiniMax, Gemini, CodeBuddy, Kilo, OpenCode Zen and more), cloud services (Azure, Cloudflare, Vertex, Bedrock, NVIDIA NIM and more) and local or self-hosted OpenAI-compatible servers behind **one local server**: a client needs one base URL and one model catalogue to call any of those models through Chat Completions, Responses or Anthropic Messages, and a multilingual Web UI manages channels and accounts, browses models, chats and shows usage."],[13111,"Hoshimi is a pure Python package: the server, the Web UI and the command line come in one distribution. The Web UI is prebuilt inside the package, so an ordinary install needs neither Node nor Bun, nor any system program."],[13061,"Hoshimi is an OpenAI- and Anthropic-compatible gateway that puts free model stations, cloud services and local models behind one API and one Web UI. This page covers what it does and how the docs are organised."],[13100,"Hoshimi is licensed under **GPL-3.0-only**. The source is on GitHub; the full text is in LICENSE."],[11819,"Hoshimi is one Python distribution, `hoshimi`; the built Web UI (`hoshimi/webui/dist/`) ships inside the wheel. The package has four layers:"],[10526,"Hoshimi keeps all of its settings and channel accounts in one JSON file, `config.json`, in the data directory. The Web UI's **Settings** and **Channels** pages, the `hoshimi config` command and the management API all change this same file. Most of the time you never need to edit it; this page is the complete reference for when you want to read or change it directly."],[8084,"Hoshimi keeps each station's native channel ids and model ids. In clients, name `channel/model`, or just the model id and let the gateway find it; see Model and account behaviour."],[10170,"Hoshimi keeps no conversation. Send the whole history with every request:"],[9993,"Hoshimi keeps no history; Claude Code sends the whole conversation every turn."],[11240,"Hoshimi publishes one distribution: the `hoshimi` wheel and sdist, both containing the built Web UI. CI runs the same checks and build for every push and pull request; when a push to a release branch changes `hoshimi/version.py`, CI publishes to PyPI **the very files that run checked and built**. The documentation site is deployed separately from the distribution."],[12045,"Hoshimi reads command output as UTF-8. Output in any other encoding never stops a command or the reply: each byte that is not UTF-8 becomes `�` (U+FFFD). Hoshimi does not, however, make commands print UTF-8; they print in the encoding of the terminal Hoshimi was started from. Where that is not UTF-8 (most often Windows set to Chinese, Japanese or Korean, whose console uses a code page such as GBK, 936), non-English file names, `dir` listings and error messages reach the model as `����`, and what `write_stdin` types (always UTF-8) is misread the same way."],[7874,"Hoshimi sends no telemetry."],[7752,"Hoshimi ships with a relay address and its signing credential, so a fresh install only needs a GitHub authorization:"],[10117,"Hoshimi speaks both the OpenAI and the Anthropic protocols. Any client that lets you set a Base URL can use it: upstream account credentials stay inside Hoshimi, and the client only needs the gateway's address, the gateway's key and a model name. This page covers what all clients have in common; the guides at the end give the exact configuration for each one."],[10062,"Hoshimi streams when a request has no `stream` field. The SDK leaves the field out when you do not pass `stream`, and `create()` then returns the raw SSE text (a `str`) instead of an object. The same holds for `client.responses.create()`."],[11370,"Hoshimi supports Python 3.10 and newer; CI lints and builds with 3.11. `.venv/` is already in `.gitignore`."],[15372,"Hoshimi treats each upstream service as a **channel** (called a provider in code and configuration, and named by an ID such as `cline`, `opencode` or `agg`). A channel holds one or more **accounts**, and the accounts of one channel form its **account pool**: requests rotate through it. This page explains those ideas and the common ways to add an account; the other pages in this section cover each kind of channel."],[7827,"Hoshimi writes no log file; logs go to the terminal running `hoshimi serve` (stderr). Redirect them when you want a file, for example `hoshimi serve 2>> hoshimi.log`; as a system service, the service manager collects them. See Data directory and migration."],[10402,"Hoshimi writes no log file: every log line goes to standard error (stderr). Once the server listens, standard output gets one line, `SERVER_READY url=http://…`, so scripts can pick up the actual address."],[2431,"Hoshimi 不保存对话。每次请求都要带上完整的历史："],[2254,"Hoshimi 不保存对话历史，Claude Code 每轮都会发送完整历史。"],[2663,"Hoshimi 不写日志文件，所有日志都输出到标准错误（stderr）。服务器开始监听后，标准输出会打印一行 `SERVER_READY url=http://…`，方便脚本获取实际地址。"],[88,"Hoshimi 不写日志文件，日志输出到运行 `hoshimi serve` 的终端（stderr）。需要文件时自己重定向，例如 `hoshimi serve 2>> hoshimi.log`；作为系统服务运行时由服务管理器收集。详见数据目录与迁移。"],[135,"Hoshimi 不发送遥测数据。"],[6974,"Hoshimi 不扫描本地端口：只有添加了账号且渠道开启，才会连接这些地址。"],[2824,"Hoshimi 不认识的顶层键和字段在读取时被忽略，并且**在下一次保存时被丢弃**，不要在文件里存放自己的备注字段。"],[330,"Hoshimi 与 pi-free 的关系：从 pi-free 搬过来时要做什么，哪些站点规则照搬了，哪些刻意没有照搬，以及运行时行为的差异。"],[345,"Hoshimi 保留各站点原生的渠道 id 和模型 id。客户端里用 `渠道/模型` 指定，或只写模型 id 由网关查找，见模型与账号行为。"],[713,"Hoshimi 先按模型路由找到渠道，再看这个渠道里能处理这个模型的账号："],[13,"Hoshimi 内置了一个中继的地址和签名凭据，全新安装只需要完成 GitHub 授权："],[3501,"Hoshimi 发布一个发行包：`hoshimi` 的 wheel 和 sdist，二者都包含构建好的 Web UI。CI 对每次推送和拉取请求做同样的检查和构建；推送到发布分支时改动了 `hoshimi/version.py`，CI 就把**同一次运行中检查过、构建过**的文件发布到 PyPI。文档站与发行包分开部署。"],[2471,"Hoshimi 向上游发出的请求（拉取模型目录、推理、登录、刷新令牌、查余额、签到）都按一条网络策略选择线路：直连，或经过某个代理。全局有一条默认策略，每个渠道可以单独覆盖。本页说明这些策略怎么写、怎么生效，以及出问题时去哪里看。"],[2115,"hoshimi 命令的组成、全局选项、命令如何读取配置、输出与 --json、退出码和日志，以及常用的命令组合。"],[2323,"Hoshimi 在请求没有 `stream` 字段时默认流式返回。SDK 在不传 `stream` 时不会发送这个字段，`create()` 会返回一段 SSE 原文（`str`）而不是对象。Responses 的 `client.responses.create()` 也一样。"],[7626,"Hoshimi 如何组织上游：渠道（供应商）、账号、账号池和模型路由，各类渠道怎样添加账号，以及怎样选择合适的渠道。"],[2378,"Hoshimi 对外提供 OpenAI 和 Anthropic 两种协议。任何能自定义 Base URL 的客户端都可以接入：上游账号的凭据留在 Hoshimi 里，客户端只需要知道网关的地址、网关的密钥和一个模型名。本页说明这些共同的约定，各客户端的具体配置见文末的指南。"],[2700,"Hoshimi 手里握着上游账号的凭据，谁能连上它，谁就能用这些账号发请求。默认配置只监听本机 `127.0.0.1`，不设任何密钥，适合只有自己使用的电脑。要让别的程序或别的机器访问时，按本页设置密钥和访问限制。"],[7635,"Hoshimi 把每个上游服务当作一个**渠道**（代码和配置中称为 provider，用一个 ID 表示，例如 `cline`、`opencode`、`agg`）。渠道下面挂着一个或多个**账号**，同一渠道的账号组成**账号池**，请求在池内轮换。本页说明这些概念和通用的添加方式；各类渠道的细节见本节其他页面。"],[2593,"Hoshimi 把配置、数据库和其他文件放在哪里，每个文件存什么、保留多久，日志去了哪里，以及如何备份、重置和从旧版本迁移。"],[4306,"Hoshimi 按 UTF-8 读取命令的输出。其他编码的输出不会让命令或回复中断：每个不是 UTF-8 的字节会变成 `�`（U+FFFD）。但 Hoshimi 不会让命令改用 UTF-8 输出，命令使用的是启动 Hoshimi 的终端的编码。终端不是 UTF-8 时（最常见的是中文、日文或韩文的 Windows，控制台使用 GBK（936）这样的代码页），中文文件名、`dir` 列表和错误信息到模型那里都会变成 `����`；`write_stdin` 输入的内容（始终是 UTF-8）也会被同样误读。"],[7045,"Hoshimi 按各服务已知的差异调整请求，例如："],[2203,"Hoshimi 按请求实际落到的账号决定怎么处理："],[3631,"Hoshimi 支持 Python 3.10 及以上；CI 的 lint 与构建使用 3.11。`.venv/` 已在 `.gitignore` 中。"],[4080,"Hoshimi 是一个 Python 发行包 `hoshimi`，Web UI 的构建产物（`hoshimi/webui/dist/`）随 wheel 一起发布。包内分四层："],[5324,"Hoshimi 是一个兼容 OpenAI 与 Anthropic 的网关：把免费模型站点、云服务和本地模型接到同一套 API 和 Web UI 后面。本页介绍它能做什么，以及文档的组织方式。"],[5328,"Hoshimi 是一个用 Python 编写的模型网关。它把免费模型站点（Cline、TRAE、ZCode、Qoder、MiniMax、Gemini、CodeBuddy、Kilo、OpenCode Zen 等）、云服务（Azure、Cloudflare、Vertex、Bedrock、NVIDIA NIM 等）和本地或自建的 OpenAI 兼容服务接到**同一个本地服务器**后面：客户端只需要一个 Base URL 和一份模型目录，就能通过 Chat Completions、Responses 或 Anthropic Messages 调用其中任何一个模型；一个多语言的 Web UI 用来管理渠道和账户、浏览模型、聊天和查看用量。"],[5374,"Hoshimi 是一个纯 Python 包，服务器、Web UI 和命令行都在同一个发行包里。Web UI 已经预先构建好放在包内，普通安装不需要 Node 或 Bun，也不需要任何系统程序。"],[2392,"Hoshimi 有两把互相独立的密钥，客户端只用其中一把："],[2180,"Hoshimi 的 `/v1/messages` 兼容 Anthropic Messages，Anthropic 官方 SDK 只需改 Base URL。模型目录与 OpenAI 接口共用，任何模型都可以通过 Messages 调用。本页示例都在本机实测过；`<model-id>` 换成 `GET /v1/models` 返回的 `id`。"],[353,"Hoshimi 的 `free` 有三个值：`true`、`false` 和 `null`（站点没有说明），不知道和收费是两回事。22 个预设中有 9 个能给出答案："],[1669,"Hoshimi 的 HTTP 接口全貌：模型接口、管理接口和 Playground 接口各在哪里、用哪把密钥，请求检查与错误格式，流式响应的约定，以及运行中服务器的 /docs 和 /openapi.json。"],[2331,"Hoshimi 的 Responses 事件流不发送 `response.content_part.added` 等内容分段事件，Python SDK 的 `client.responses.stream()` 辅助方法依赖这些事件，会抛出 `IndexError`。请改用上面的 `responses.create(..., stream=True)`。"],[1117,"Hoshimi 的 Responses 是无状态的：请求被转换成 Chat Completions，交给与 Chat 相同的路由，结果再转换回 Responses 格式。每次都要在 `input` 中发送完整的对话。"],[3086,"Hoshimi 的代码分四层，依赖只朝一个方向：`api` 和 `cli` 依赖 `core`，`core` 不依赖它们，也不导入任何框架。两个入口——服务器和命令行——都通过 `build_services()` 得到同一个 `Services`，再各自把它包装成 HTTP 路由或命令。本页先讲分层规则，再讲 `Services`、应用工厂和错误，最后跟随一个请求走完全程。"],[2787,"Hoshimi 的全部设置和渠道账号都保存在数据目录中的一个 JSON 文件 `config.json` 里。网页界面的 **设置** 和 **渠道** 页、`hoshimi config` 命令和管理 API 改的都是这同一个文件。大多数情况下不需要手动编辑它；本页是给需要直接查看或修改它的人准备的完整参考。"],[3801,"Hoshimi 的各类检查：pytest 的布局与共享夹具、写渠道和路由测试的方式、Web UI 的 Vitest 规则测试、生成类型的检查、在真实浏览器里查横向溢出的 check_layout.py，以及 CI 怎样运行它们。"],[3613,"Hoshimi 的开发环境由两部分组成：一个以可编辑方式安装了 Hoshimi 及其开发依赖的 Python 环境，以及用来安装、构建和测试 Web UI 与本文档站的 bun。日常任务都通过 `scripts/dev.py` 运行：它只用标准库，在 Linux、macOS 和 Windows 上行为一致，运行的也正是 CI 运行的那些工具。"],[2604,"Hoshimi 的所有状态都在一个数据目录里：配置文件、记录用量和对话的数据库，以及少数几个给人或其他程序读的文件。搬家、备份或重置时只需要处理这一个文件夹。"],[1676,"Hoshimi 的服务器同时提供三组接口和网页界面，默认地址是 `http://127.0.0.1:10600`。本页说明它们共同的规则；每组接口的字段见各自的参考页。"],[1838,"hoshimi 的每一条命令：作用、参数与选项及其默认值、输出格式、--json 的字段和示例，内容取自各命令的 --help 与源码。"],[3811,"Hoshimi 的测试不访问网络，也不需要任何真实的渠道凭据：上游由假的渠道或 `httpx.MockTransport` 代替，每个测试都有自己的临时数据目录。提交前运行一次 `python scripts/dev.py check`，它覆盖 CI 的 Python 与 Web UI 检查。"],[2024,"Hoshimi 的设置都在 `config.json` 里，环境变量只决定两件事：**数据放在哪里**和**日志有多详细**。此外，它在选择默认数据目录和代理时会读取几个通用的系统变量。本页列出全部变量。"],[5613,"Hoshimi 第一次启动、还没有任何配置时，`opencode`（OpenCode Zen）和 `kilo`（Kilo AI）两个渠道就已经可用：它们带一个不含凭据的占位账号，直接向上游的免费模型发请求。在 **渠道** 页面上，这两个渠道显示 **无需账户**。"],[2015,"Hoshimi 自己的变量"],[2462,"Hoshimi 访问上游站点时走哪条线路：自动读取环境代理、直连或指定代理，按渠道覆盖，哪些请求受影响，以及如何读网络诊断。"],[2014,"Hoshimi 读取的全部环境变量：它自己的 HOSHIMI_DATA_DIR 与 HOSHIMI_LOG_LEVEL、决定默认数据目录和代理的标准变量、云 SDK 读取的凭据变量、Playground 工具运行命令时设置的变量，以及它刻意不读取的变量。"],[2019,"Hoshimi 还会读取的系统变量"],[5363,"Hoshimi 采用 **GPL-3.0-only** 许可证，源码在 GitHub，许可证全文见 LICENSE。"],[4124,"Hoshimi 采用的分层 Python + Vue 骨架，`scripts/dev.py` 也由它而来"],[3791,"hoshimi-dev.netlify.app"],[11530,"hoshimi-dev.netlify.app"],[9919,"Hoshimi's `/v1/messages` is compatible with Anthropic Messages, so the official Anthropic SDKs only need a different Base URL. The model catalogue is the same one the OpenAI endpoints use, and any model can be called through Messages. Every example here was run against a local server; replace `<model-id>` with an `id` from `GET /v1/models`."],[8092,"Hoshimi's `free` has three values: `true`, `false` and `null` (the station did not say); unknown is not the same as paid. Nine of the 22 presets can give an answer:"],[10825,"Hoshimi's code has four layers, and dependencies run one way: `api` and `cli` depend on `core`; `core` depends on neither and imports no framework. Both entry points, the server and the command line, get the same `Services` from `build_services()` and wrap it in HTTP routes or commands of their own. This page covers the layering rule first, then `Services`, the app factory and errors, and finally follows one request all the way through."],[9754,"Hoshimi's own variables"],[8856,"Hoshimi's Responses is stateless: the request is converted to Chat Completions, routed exactly like Chat, and the result converted back to the Responses format. Send the whole conversation in `input` every time."],[10070,"Hoshimi's Responses stream sends no content-part events such as `response.content_part.added`. The Python SDK's `client.responses.stream()` helper relies on them and raises `IndexError`. Use `responses.create(..., stream=True)` as above."],[9415,"Hoshimi's server offers three groups of endpoints next to the Web UI, at `http://127.0.0.1:10600` by default. This page covers the rules they share; each group's fields are on its own reference page."],[9763,"Hoshimi's settings live in `config.json`; environment variables decide only two things: **where the data lives** and **how much is logged**. Beyond that, a few standard system variables are read to choose the default data folder and proxies. This page lists them all."],[11550,"Hoshimi's tests never touch the network and need no real provider credentials: upstreams are replaced by a fake provider or by `httpx.MockTransport`, and every test gets a temporary data folder of its own. Run `python scripts/dev.py check` once before committing: it covers CI's Python and Web UI checks."],[1739,"Host"],[9478,"Host"],[12820,"Host and origin checks apply to requests with a key too; a key does not get around them. The detailed rules are in Access and security."],[10249,"Host names without a dot"],[2691,"Host 检查"],[9816,"Hosts listed in `NO_PROXY` are reached directly: host names, domain suffixes, hosts with a port, CIDR networks, or `*` (everything direct), separated by commas or semicolons."],[12929,"Hourly detail is kept for 120 days. An older day shows **Hour-by-hour detail is not kept for this day. The totals above still include it.**"],[8364,"Hourly totals"],[10385,"Hourly totals"],[12997,"Hourly totals"],[12891,"Hours"],[12894,"Hours"],[12897,"Hours"],[8373,"Hours and dates follow the server's local time."],[10409,"How"],[11528,"How"],[12037,"How a command runs"],[12475,"How a reply ended"],[9173,"How a reply ended (`streaming` while it runs)"],[9281,"How a stream ends:"],[9957,"How Claude Code's requests are handled"],[10742,"How Cline signs in: `sdk` (default, device-code authorization) or `extension` (browser authorization with a local callback on ports 48801–48811). New accounts record the method used; a change affects later logins only"],[9857,"How commands work"],[14685,"How each backend is handled"],[8774,"How each station signs in is covered in Channels."],[9062,"How full the context window is, and what the replies took"],[15363,"How Hoshimi organises upstreams: channels (providers), accounts, account pools and model routing, how each kind of channel gets its accounts, and how to choose one."],[8069,"How Hoshimi relates to pi-free: what to do when moving over from pi-free, which station rules were carried across, which were deliberately left out, and how runtime behaviour differs."],[11440,"How it is organised"],[12540,"How it is sent"],[7944,"How level names map:"],[9197,"How long a reply worked, less the time it waited for approvals; and that wait. `0` for replies kept before this was counted"],[12474,"How long a reply works"],[11046,"How long an account cools down after a station's safety block"],[11043,"How long an account cools down when its allowance ran out and the upstream named no time"],[12276,"How long an account rests follows the reset time the station gives, or an hour when it gives none. Holds are kept in memory and cleared by a restart. The full rotation and retry rules are in Models and reasoning effort."],[12881,"How long data is kept"],[8271,"How long records are kept"],[9395,"How long replies worked; Unix seconds a reply has been running since, or `null`"],[12308,"How many 401/403s"],[12306,"How many 429s"],[12310,"How many 5xx"],[12683,"How many accounts a request may rotate through before it fails; at least 1. The rotation rules are in Models and reasoning effort"],[12439,"How many accounts it has, or **No account needed** (an anonymous channel, such as OpenCode Zen and Kilo)."],[8311,"How many accounts were asked until one answered (including retries after a back-off); 0 when none answered"],[12135,"How many files changed and the lines added and removed, then each file with what happened to it (**Added**, **Modified**, **Renamed from** *path*, **Deleted**) and its diff, highlighted in the file's language. Once applied, each line has its numbers in the file before and after. A long diff starts folded. A patch shows while the model is still writing it"],[12440,"How many models in the catalogue come from it (once the catalogue has loaded)."],[12915,"How many of them were reasoning"],[12912,"How many were uncached and how many written to cache"],[7877,"How model names are routed"],[7876,"How model names are routed to channels, how catalogues are discovered and cached, how capabilities and reasoning effort shape the request, availability probes, and how failures lead to account rotation, retries, renewal and quota records."],[12513,"How much of the context window is used and left, the last request's and the whole conversation's tokens (cached ones among them), compactions, how long replies worked, and the tools"],[12345,"How the catalogue loads"],[10525,"How the file is written"],[8267,"How the gateway records each call: which fields, where token and cache counts come from, how speed is measured, how long records are kept, how to query them, and the live event stream."],[9854,"How the hoshimi command is organised, its global options, how commands read the configuration, output and --json, exit codes and logging, and common command sequences."],[13010,"How the model catalogue loads"],[11338,"How the site is organised, written and built locally is in Documentation site."],[11671,"How the Vue app is built and laid out, types generated from OpenAPI, data fetching and the live connection, i18n, theme and design tokens, layers and motion, and the layout rules the tests enforce."],[13005,"How the Web UI is laid out: the navigation, live activity in the top bar, signing in with the access key, language and appearance, and the guide to each page."],[14787,"How thinking levels are sent differs by service (a menu appears only when the catalogue says the model thinks):"],[10985,"How to add a provider: the Provider contract, the normalized chunk protocol, error classification and account rotation, catalogues and capabilities, and interactive login flows."],[15371,"How to choose"],[9451,"How to send it"],[10135,"How to send it"],[10443,"How to send it"],[7855,"How to turn it off"],[15115,"How to use each sign-in station adapter: Cline, Gemini Code Assist, ZCode, MiniMax, TRAE, Qoder, CodeBuddy/WorkBuddy, CodeArts, Loomy, Raccoon, LobsterAI, Codex, EAC and Zhipu — how to sign in, what each offers and its limits."],[8242,"HTML instead 