,"If none has it and only one provider is enabled, the name goes to that provider as is."],[9641,"If the address is not a loopback address (`127.*`, `localhost`, `::1`), a warning is printed. Without a tool access key the server refuses to start (exit code 4); without a model API key it warns that external model APIs accept requests without a key. `security.allow_cidrs` must also be configured, or the server refuses to start (exit code 4). See Security."],[8265,"If the problem remains, open a report on GitHub Issues with logs taken with `HOSHIMI_LOG_LEVEL=DEBUG`, the output of `hoshimi version` and the steps to reproduce. Logs can contain account ids and host names; check them before sharing."],[8453,"If the provider has a Messages endpoint of its own for them (models whose protocol is Messages on a regular API provider, such as `anthropic` or `minimax-api`), the request is **forwarded natively**, rotating across those accounts."],[12150,"If the reply had already ended, the message goes back in the box (\"The reply had already ended; your message is back in the box.\") for you to send as a new message. If the reply is stopped or fails before reading it, the text comes back to the box too."],[8954,"If the result is still not on the menu, the model's default level is used. The chosen level is written into the upstream request the way the model declares; the output ceiling is then the smaller of the model's capacity and the request's own value, whatever the level."],[12092,"If the reviewer denies 3 calls in a row, or 10 in one reply, the reply is stopped: the calls left in that round are marked **Stopped**, and the reply ends with \"The automatic review denied *n* of this reply’s calls, so it was stopped. Say how to go on, or choose another approval mode.\""],[12164,"If the server is reachable from other machines, anyone who can sign in to the Web UI can use these tools. Set an access key and limit who can connect (see Access and security)."],[13173,"If the service has