 middle of a longer output is cut, keeping the start and the end."],[12073,"In **Automatic review**, the calls that would ask in **Ask first** go to a model instead of to you: every `shell` and `exec_command`, `write_stdin` when it types something, every `apply_patch`, and `read` outside the workspace. The reviewer is **Settings › Tools › How tools run › Review model** (`playground.review_model`); empty, the default, is **The chat’s own model**. A fast, careful model is a good choice."],[11176,"In `catalog.py`, write a `<id>_spec(model_id, provider)` for the station, with context, images, thinking and reasoning-effort choices."],[11177,"In `credential_forms()` of `core/provider_forms.py`, say which fields adding an account asks for (`zhipu` needs only `api_key`). The Web UI's **Add account** dialog and the management API both read it; list only fields the adapter actually accepts."],[14779,"In `fireworks` and `opencode-go`, models whose name starts with `claude` use Messages; in `opencode-go`, models starting with `gemini-` use the native Gemini protocol."],[11614,"In `hoshimi/webui`, `bun run test` runs Vitest and `bun run typecheck` runs vue-tsc; `python scripts/dev.py test-web` runs both in turn. The environment is happy-dom; `src/test/setup.ts` supplies the `ElementInternals` that `@material/web` asks for, and `src/test/motion-zero.css` sets every motion duration to zero, so a test never waits on a transition. Vitest uses the `vmThreads` pool (worker threads race each other creating their temporary folder on Windows)."],[11175,"In `providers/factory.py`, add the class to `PROVIDER_CLASSES` and put the ID at the right place in `PROVIDER_ORDER`. That order decides which provider a bare model name is looked up in first, and the order keyless providers start in."],[11473,"In `site/content/docs/`, create `<slug>.mdx` (Chinese) and `<slug>.en.mdx` (English). Slugs are lowercase with hyphens, prefixed by their section (`guide-`, `clients-`, `providers-`, `cli-`, `config-`, `advanced-`, `api-`, `development-`). Both files have the same structure: the same sections in the same order, the same code blocks and links. The Chinese is natural Simplified Chinese, not a word-for-word translation; the English is plain and direct."],[8548,"In `usage`, `input_tokens` excludes the cache; cache reads and writes are in `cache_read_input_tokens` and `cache_creation_input_tokens`."],[9939,"In a multi-turn conversation, send the assistant's `thinking` / `redacted_thinking` blocks back with their original `signature`. Do not edit or invent signatures, and do not reuse one model's signature with another."],[8551,"In a multi-turn conversation, the client sends the assistant's `thinking` / `redacted_thinking` blocks back with their original signatures and tool calls:"],[11776,"In a row pairing a name with a control, the text element has `min-width: 0` (the test lists the components and selectors)"],[11269,"in a temporary data folder it builds the app and, through `TestClient`, requests `/health`, the home page (which must contain \"Hoshimi\"), every file under `assets/` and `/api/v1/providers`, and checks there is a favicon."],[14783,"In Chat requests, `max_completion_tokens` becomes `max_tokens` (`minimax-chat` and `wandb` use `max_completion_tokens` instead); services that do not accept the `developer` role get `system`."],[11324,"In the `pypi` environment, downloads the `distributions` artifact and runs `twine upload dist/* --skip-existing --non-interactive`"],[9099,"In the archive"],[7825,"In the data directory: `~/.local/share/hoshimi` on Linux, `~/Library/Application Support/hoshimi` on macOS, `%APPDATA%\\hoshimi` on Windows; `HOSHIMI_DATA_DIR` moves it elsewhere. `config.json` holds the settings and accounts; `hoshimi.db` holds usage, check-ins, probe verdicts and Playground conversations."],[10079,"In the Playground, **Copy as API request** in a reply's **More actions** menu copies the Chat Completions request behind that reply as a curl comma