ler `max_tokens` from the caller, but never below 512; so with an explicit level, a caller limit below 512 is raised to 512. For menu models the minimum is 1."],[11762,"The language preference defaults to `auto`, which follows the browser's first language (`zh*` is Simplified Chinese, `ja*` Japanese, anything else English) and updates when the system language changes."],[10875,"The last availability verdict per model"],[12275,"The last renewal failed; the next round tries again"],[10390,"The latest"],[7922,"The latest availability probe verdict"],[8748,"The latest availability verdict, or `null` if never probed"],[8648,"The latest availability verdicts"],[8158,"The latest network result per channel and operation; see Network and proxies"],[8640,"The latest outcome of each kind of network operation per provider"],[10394,"The latest per model"],[7778,"The latest token in `eac-user.json`, read on every request, so a new login applies at once"],[11863,"The layered Python + Vue skeleton Hoshimi follows; `scripts/dev.py` comes from it too"],[10811,"The layering rule"],[11619,"The layout rules: rows that can shrink, bounded lists, scrolling only through `.app-scroll`, scrollbar lanes, the bottom navigation, unstretched charts; see Web UI"],[7939,"The level is chosen and the patch the model declares is merged into the body (for example `reasoning_effort`, or `thinking` and `output_config.effort`); `max_tokens` becomes the smaller of the model's output limit and the caller's limit"],[13405,"The level is sent in the `reasoning_effort` field."],[12906,"The line under it"],[12436,"The line under the list says whether a tool access key is set: **A tool access key is required to manage this server.** or **No tool access key is set.**. With no tool access key, the title also has **API reference**, which opens the server's own API documentation (`/docs`) in a new tab. With a key the button is left out, because that page cannot send the key the browser keeps; reach `/docs` and `/ope