ts the daily timer only: **Done · time** when today's timed check-in got through, **Not yet today** otherwise."],[12643,"The system prompt is empty by default, so a model gets only the conversation and the tool descriptions. The prompt below gives it the rest: when to act and when to ask, how to use the tools well, how to take approvals, steering and compaction, and how its reply is rendered here. Paste it into **Settings › General › Playground › System prompt**. It suits chats with and without tools, and any model; replies follow the language the user writes in."],[9674,"The table has **Model** and **Provider** columns. A model id offered by several channels is listed once, under the channel that comes first."],[9680,"The table's columns are **Id**, **Name**, **Accounts** and **Models**; switched-off channels are listed under it as `disabled: …`. The account count leaves out the built-in anonymous identity of the anonymous channels."],[9688,"The table's columns are **Id**, **Name**, **Base URL** and **Key env**, followed by a usage hint:"],[11331,"The tag runs CI once more: it checks the tag against the version, skips the files PyPI already has, then creates a GitHub release with the distributions and generated notes."],[11357,"The task runner; see below"],[13410,"The terminal prints a verification link and a code (in the Web UI, click **Sign in**; the dialog shows the **Verification code**). Confirm in the browser and the account is written to `config.json`. Kilo returns a long-lived key, not a renewable OAuth token, so it is never renewed on a timer."],[8147,"The terminal running `hoshimi serve`"],[11745,"The test environment: `setup.ts` (gives happy-dom an `ElementInternals`), `motion-zero.css` (every motion duration at zero)"],[11179,"The test layout and shared fixtures are in Testing."],[9231,"The text. A message needs text or an attachment (`400` otherwise)"],[9167,"The text. For a reply that used tools, its text steps joined by blank lines"],[13314,"The thinking-level menu, in display order. Including `disabled` makes thinking switchable off."],[10633,"The three keys also accept the singular spellings `allow_cidr`, `allow_host` and `allow_origin`, and a single comma-separated string instead of a list. A save writes them back as plural lists. The checks are described in Access control."],[12965,"The time for today's calls, the date for older ones; hover for the full time"],[7849,"The timer starts only when the server starts, and turning the switch off while it runs does not stop it. Also, `hoshimi serve` overrides the setting at start with `--refresh/--no-refresh` (on by default), and `--checkin/--no-checkin` likewise. To turn them off, start with `hoshimi serve --no-refresh` or `--no-checkin`."],[8225,"The timers start only when the server starts. `hoshimi serve` turns both on by default and overrides `server.auto_refresh` and `server.auto_checkin` from the configuration; to turn them off, start with `--no-refresh` or `--no-checkin`."],[12271,"The token has expired"],[15437,"The tokens of many sign-in stations expire. With **Credential renewal** on (`server.auto_refresh`, on by default) the gateway checks every 30 minutes and renews accounts that expire within the hour or record no expiry. With **Daily check-in** on (`server.auto_checkin`, on by default) it claims each supporting station's free credits once a day, by the calendar day in UTC+8. Which stations support renewal, check-in and balance queries is listed in Free stations."],[10494,"The tool access key is for you, to manage the gateway; the model API key is for the other clients on your LAN (editor plugins, agents)."],[11895,"The tool access key protects the Web UI and the management API (`/api/v1/*`, `/docs`, `/openapi.json`); the model API `/v1/*` is protected by a separate, independent **Model API key**. The Playground goes through the management API, so it needs only the tool access key. The two keys and LAN access are covered in Security."],[12642,"The tool settings (`playground.tools`, `workspace`, `approval`, `search_url`) are in Playground tools."],[10096,"The top-level `model` is the default model as `provider/model`, where the provider is `hoshimi`."],[11872,"The two default anonymous channels"],[13336,"The two free lanes that are on by default and need no account, OpenCode Zen and Kilo: what they offer, how to turn them off, how a key widens the catalogue, and how their protocols are handled."],[10425,"The two keys"],[10456,"The two keys are independent: the tool access key does not open `/v1/*`, and the model API key does not open `/api/*`."],[7746,"The two relay modes"],[11803,"The unit tests read the source; sideways overflow in real browsers is checked by `scripts/check_layout.py`, see Testing."],[10299,"The upstream answered with a Cloudflare challenge (`cf-mitigated: challenge`)"],[8238,"The upstream answered with a Cloudflare challenge. Hoshimi does not solve challenges; try another route or later"],[9520,"The upstream failed"],[8920,"The upstream failed; `response.error` says why"],[8734,"The upstream protocol: `chat`, `responses`, `messages` and so on"],[9528,"The upstream refused the account's credentials"],[8209,"The upstream rejected this account's refresh token (log: `<channel>/<account>: refresh token rejected, account needs a new login`). The account leaves rotation and renewal skips it until you sign in again:"],[8333,"The upstream reported no token usage"],[10032,"The upstream returned an error after the stream began, Hoshimi ended the stream with an error event, and Codex gave up after reconnecting a few times. Open the **Usage** page to read the call's error. In local tests the same tool-calling task finished on some models while others were refused by the upstream with `HTTP 400` on the second turn; another model usually works"],[9534,"The upstream's `404` / `410`"],[8926,"The upstream's model name; a name several providers share is listed once (the first provider in order)"],[9526,"The upstream's status"],[9530,"The upstream's status"],[9522,"The upstream's status (usually `429`)"],[12873,"The Usage page: choose a range or a single day, read the headline tiles and the token and speed charts, break usage down by model, provider, account and API, and look at each call."],[9325,"The user or the review model denied it; it did not run. Denied by the review model, `output` is what the model was told; denied by the user, it is empty"],[13501,"The values are `chat`, `responses` and `messages`, with the aliases `openai-completions`, `openai-responses` and `anthropic-messages` also accepted. `google` and `google-vertex` use `gemini` or `chat`. Set these only for protocols the upstream really supports. More protocol-related options are in Local and compatible endpoints."],[12363,"The verdict of the last probe, below; **Not probed** for a model no round has reached"],[8616,"The version"],[8689,"The version"],[11225,"The version"],[11707,"The Vite dev server (port 5173)"],[11833,"The Vue 3 + Vite interface; `dist/` ships in the package"],[11809,"The way in for contributors: what Hoshimi is made of, what is authoritative, the conventions that apply everywhere, and what each development page covers."],[11373,"The Web UI (`hoshimi/webui/`) and the documentation site (`site/`) both use bun to install, build and test; CI uses bun 1.4.2. When `bun` is not on `PATH`, `dev.py` prints one line saying so and exits with status 127 rather than a traceback."],[8170,"The Web UI build files are missing and only the API is served. Packages installed from PyPI include the build; when running from source, build the Web UI first; see Development setup."],[10917,"The Web UI derives its root from the URL of its own script, so it needs no change under a prefix."],[11687,"The Web UI lives in `hoshimi/webui/`: a Vue 3 + Vite + TypeScript app following the Material Design 3 system it shares with its sister project Mizuoto. It talks to the server over HTTP only; the built `dist/` ships in the Python package and the server serves it as static files. This page covers its structure, its contract with the server, and the rules a change to the interface must keep, most of them enforced by tests under `src/`."],[11346,"The Web UI: bun"],[7901,"The Web UI's **Models** page and the Playground load the catalogue through `GET /api/v1/catalog/stream` (SSE): cached results come first, then each channel's fresh result as it arrives. At most 8 fetches run at once; a round waits at most 20 seconds, marks unfinished channels as timed out and keeps the models already received. The standard `/v1/models` stays plain JSON."],[7826,"The Web UI's **Settings** › **About** also shows the **Data directory**, **Config file** and **Database**."],[10356,"the Web UI's **Settings** › **About** shows the **Data directory**, **Config file** and **Database**;"],[10540,"The Web UI's **Settings** and **Channels** pages, or `PATCH /api/v1/settings`"],[8999,"The Web UI's Playground does everything through these routes, so a script can do the same: keep conversations, stream replies, run the tools and answer their approvals. Everything a model is sent (the system prompt, file text, image descriptions, earlier tool calls) is put together on the server; a client only says what to add and where."],[11852,"The Web UI's TypeScript types are generated from the server's OpenAPI document (`src/api/schema.d.ts`) and committed; CI regenerates them and fails on a difference. A change to a management API model means running `python scripts/dev.py typegen` and committing the result."],[12977,"The whole call"],[10805,"The whole configuration is validated before writing, so set keys that depend on each other in one go. To switch to proxy mode, for example, set the whole `network` object; `network.mode proxy` on its own is refused for lack of a proxy URL."],[12500,"The whole conversation scrolls as one. A tool's output, a compaction summary and a question being edited scroll on their own when they are long; once one reaches its top or its end, scrolling on in the same direction (the wheel, a trackpad or a swipe) moves the conversation instead of stopping there."],[8837,"The whole conversation; Hoshimi keeps no history"],[9408,"The whole of Hoshimi's HTTP interface: where the model, management and Playground APIs live and which key each uses, request checks and error shapes, streaming conventions, and the running server's /docs and /openapi.json."],[12021,"The whole patch is worked out against the files before anything is written: if one hunk does not apply, no file is changed."],[12154,"The workspace is the line the approval modes draw: reading or changing files outside it asks in **Ask first** and **Ask outside the workspace**, and goes to the review model in **Automatic review**. It is not a boundary for commands: a command can `cd` anywhere and touch anything the user running Hoshimi can."],[12153,"The workspace is where the tools start: relative paths resolve there, and `shell` and background commands run there unless the model names another folder. It is **Settings › Tools › How tools run › Workspace** (`playground.workspace`; `~` is expanded); empty uses `workspace` in the data folder (see Data folder and paths). It is created when a reply with tools first runs."],[11678,"Theme and design tokens"],[11270,"There are four workflows in `.github/workflows/`:"],[13409,"There are two ways to add a Kilo account:"],[12156,"There is no sandbox. Tools run as the user running Hoshimi, on that machine, with its files, credentials and network."],[15134,"These channels correspond to the free, trial or subscription allowances of AI coding tools and platforms. Most of these stations do not hand out an API key you can paste; they issue tokens through a browser sign-in. Hoshimi performs the sign-in in place of the official client, stores the credential as an account, and takes care of renewal and check-in."],[8816,"These endpoints serve OpenAI-compatible clients at `http://127.0.0.1:10600/v1`, authenticated with the model API key (see API overview). Usage examples are in OpenAI SDKs and curl."],[8172,"These errors come from Hoshimi's own access control; the request never reached upstream. Their body looks like `{\"code\": \"…\", \"message\": \"…\", \"detail\": {}}`. An OpenAI-shaped `{\"error\": {…}}` is an error from upstream or from routing instead; see the sections below."],[13384,"These IDs use the thinking menus declared by the reference implementation; other IDs follow the shared capability table (see Model behaviour)."],[15337,"These key-billed services also support `hoshimi login`; see their pages for details:"],[9637,"These options apply to this start only and are not written to `config.json`. An empty string for `--access-token`, `--model-api-key` or `--default-model` has no effect; the configured value is kept."],[12846,"These options are kept in the current browser and affect only it:"],[8456,"These provider options (in `providers.<id>.options`) adjust the behaviour:"],[11855,"These repositories sit as local clones in the repository root, to compare protocols and behaviour against. They are all in `.gitignore`: they never enter this repository and Hoshimi does not depend on them."],[14723,"These services' addresses, protocols and catalogue endpoints are built in, so an account needs only a key."],[15112,"These translations make requests acceptable to NIM; they are not full OpenAI feature parity. Whether a request succeeds is finally decided by the key's permissions, quota and model access."],[8437,"These two endpoints are compatible with Anthropic Messages and serve clients such as the Anthropic SDKs and Claude Code. The base address is `http://127.0.0.1:10600` (clients add `/v1/messages` themselves), authenticated with the model API key sent as `x-api-key` or `Authorization: Bearer` (see API overview). Usage examples are in Anthropic SDK."],[9825,"These variables must be in the environment of the process that runs Hoshimi, 